hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3601","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Sijzi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Sufyan, a man of the market people, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man of the Emigrants shall remain in Makkah after completing the rites beyond three days. This Sufyan from whom Sufyan al-Thawri narrated is Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"3602","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Hafs al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim is he from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is he who abandons what Allah Almighty forbade. None narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mu'tamir; Isma'il ibn Hafs is alone in it."
"3603","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ..."
"3604","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub and Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, as Hammad reckons, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man will meet his father on the Day of Resurrection and say: O father, what kind of son was I to you? He will say: The best son. He will say: Will you obey me today in something I command you? He will say: Yes. He will say: Take my hand. So he takes his hand and goes with him until he comes to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, while He is presenting creation. He will say: Son of Adam, enter through whichever gates of Paradise you wish. He will say: O Lord, and my father with me, for You promised me You would not disgrace me. He, Blessed and Exalted, will turn away from him and turn to creation, presenting them; then He will turn to him and say: Son of Adam, enter through whichever gates of Paradise you wish. He will say: O Lord, and my father with me, for You promised me You would not disgrace me. He, Blessed and Exalted, will turn away from him and turn to creation, presenting them. He will say: Son of Adam, enter through whichever gates of Paradise you wish. He will say: O Lord, and my father with me, for You promised me You would not disgrace me. So Allah will transform his father into a coarse hyena, and he will be cast into the Fire; he will take by its forelock and say: Is this your father? He will say: No, by Your might, this is not my father. Muhammad ibn Sirin said: We used to narrate that it was Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3605","Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ahwazi al-Adl narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Mukhtar al-Tammar, from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi, from his father, he said: I saw Ali perform ablution from the Taym water vessel, three times three, and say: This is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). None narrated this hadith from Abu Hayyan al-Taymi except Mukhtar al-Tammar, and he is Mukhtar ibn Nafi'."
"3606","Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Imran ibn Anas al-Makki, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mention the good qualities of your dead, and refrain from their evils. None narrated this hadith from Ata except Imran ibn Anas."
"3607","Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Dinar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: Allah Almighty looked into the hearts of servants and found the heart of Muhammad the best of servants' hearts; then He looked into the hearts of servants after the heart of Muhammad and found the hearts of his companions the best of servants' hearts, so He chose them for His religion, fighting for His religion. Whatever the Muslims deem good is good with Allah, and whatever they deem evil is evil with Allah."
"3608","Those named Zayd: Zayd ibn al-Muhtadi Abu Habib al-Marrudhi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talqani narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Harun narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded regarding sandals and the ring. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Umar ibn Harun; Sa'id ibn Ya'qub is alone in it."
"3609","Those named Zubayr: al-Zubayr ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Asim ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with two pouches in his hand: one of gold and the other of silk, and said: These two are forbidden for the males of my ummah, lawful for its females. None narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Amr ibn Jarir; Dawud ibn Sulayman is alone in it."
"3610","Chapter of Sin, those named Sa'd: Sa'd ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the mu'adhdhins. None narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Zuhayr, nor narrated it from Zuhayr except Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi."
"3611","Those named Sa'dun: Sa'dun ibn Suhayl ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhu'ayb al-Akkawi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Firas ibn Yahya, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother. None narrated this hadith from Firas except Shayban."
"3612","Those named Sa'id: Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Khalaf al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim al-Ijli narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching, a man came stepping over people's necks until he sat near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah finished his prayer he said: What prevented you, O so-and-so, from joining the congregation? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was keen to place myself in the place you see. He said: I saw you stepping over the necks of Muslims and harming them; whoever harms a Muslim has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah. None narrated this hadith from Anas ibn Malik except al-Qasim al-Ijli, nor from al-Qasim except Musa ibn Khalaf; Sa'id ibn Sulayman is alone in it."
"3613","Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only combined Hajj and Umrah because he knew he would not go out after that. None narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Yazid ibn Ata."
"3614","Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar, from Ibn Shihab, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibn Mujabbar, and it is not narrated from Sa'd except with this chain."
"3615","Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of happiness is a righteous wife, a righteous dwelling and a righteous mount; and part of misery is an evil wife, an evil mount and an evil dwelling. None narrated this hadith from al-Abbas ibn Dharih except Ibrahim ibn Uthman, and he is Abu Shaybah."
"3616","Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate, saying: O Allah, make the widest of Your provision upon me at my old age and the end of my life. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the hadith of al-Qasim, from A'ishah."
"3617","Sa'id ibn Isra'il al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Musa al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Urwah, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of a woman's blessing is the ease of her engagement and the ease of her dowry. Urwah said: And I say: part of her first ill-omen is the abundance of her dowry. None narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Usamah ibn Zayd; Ibn al-Mubarak is alone in it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3618","Sa'id ibn Aws al-Dimashqi the cobbler narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters a horse between two horses, while he is safe from being outrun, it is gambling. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Bashir, nor from Sa'id except al-Walid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in it."
"3619","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari, from Abu Zabyah, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love is from Allah, and repute is in heaven; when Allah loves a servant, Jibril calls out: Your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him. Then love for him is placed on earth. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Sharik is alone in it."
"3620","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yusuf al-Shami narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Delay by the rich is injustice, and when you are referred to one solvent, accept the transfer. None narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, nor from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali except Yazid ibn Yusuf; Zahmawayh is alone in it."
"3621","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, he said: Ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Judges are three: a man who judges and strives and is right, so for him is Paradise; a man who judges and strives and errs, so for him is Paradise; and a man who judges unjustly, so he is in the Fire. None narrated this hadith from Abu Hashim al-Rummani except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"3622","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ibrahim ibn Jarir, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his boots, not removing them, and pray in them. It was said to him: After the revelation of al-Ma'idah? He said: Yes."
"3623","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My ummah will remain upon fitrah as long as they pray Fajr at its bright time."
"3624","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Abu Salamah, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the boots."
"3625","Sa'id ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rooster, for it calls to prayer at its time."
"3626","3621 - Sa'id ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Awn narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman informed us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gates of heaven are opened for five: for the recitation of the Qur'an, for the meeting of the two armies, for the falling of rain, for the supplication of the oppressed, and for the adhan. None narrated these hadiths from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' except Hafs ibn Sulayman; 'Amr ibn 'Awn alone transmitted them."
"3627","3622 - Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Salm ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakrah Abu Hammam al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar al-Khattabi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Majid ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not abandon foul speech and lying, Allah has no need for him to abandon his food and drink. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except 'Abd al-Majid; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar al-Khattabi alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"3628","3623 - Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Dhari' al-Basri narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Ali al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from al-Harith, from 'Ali: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in the Fajr prayer at Tanzil al-Sajdah. None narrated this hadith from 'Amr ibn Murrah except Layth, nor from Layth except Mu'tamir; 'Amr ibn 'Ali alone transmitted it."
"3629","3624 - Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umarah al-Ansari, known as Ibn al-Qaddah - I heard from him in Baghdad - narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: Our arrival to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was five years after the Hijrah; we set out seeking connection through Quraysh in the year of the Confederates, I being with my brother al-Fadl, and with us our servant Abu Rafi', until we reached al-'Arj, then we turned off from his riding route and took that road via al-Jathjathah, until we came out to Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, until we entered Madinah, and we found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Trench; I was then eight years old and my brother thirteen years old. None narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn al-Husayn except his son Sulayman; 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Umarah alone transmitted it."
"3630","3625 - Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Isa al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. None narrated this hadith from Yunus except 'Abd Allah ibn 'Isa; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi alone transmitted it."
"3631","3626 - Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Bishr - the maternal brother of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi - narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on one of his journeys with some of his Companions, the prayer came, and the people found no water to perform ablution with, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, we find no water to perform ablution with. So a man from the people went and brought a small cup of water; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, then spread his fingers over the cup, and all the people performed ablution until they reached what they wanted. And Anas was unsure how many they were, about seventy. None narrated this hadith from Yunus except Mahbub ibn al-Hasan; Habib ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"3632","3627 - Sa'id ibn 'Abd Rabbih al-Saffar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Tha'lab narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I missed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night from his bed, and I thought he had gone to his slave-girl Mariyah, so I got up feeling the wall, and found him standing praying; I put my hand in his hair to see whether he had bathed or not. When he finished, he said: Has your devil seized you, O 'A'ishah? I said: Do I have a devil, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. I said: And all the children of Adam? He said: Yes. I said: And you? He said: Yes, but Allah helped me against him, so he submitted. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, except Faraj ibn Fudalah."
"3633","3628 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two whose prayer does not pass beyond their heads: a slave who has fled from his masters until he returns to them, and a woman who disobeyed her husband until she returns. None narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd, nor did anyone narrate it from 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd except Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir; Ibn Abi Safwan alone transmitted it."
"3634","3629 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir Abu Ghassan al-'Anbari narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn al-Jahm Abu 'Uthman the muezzin narrated to us, he said: Khuza'i ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: We were sitting with 'Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal, and he narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not shoot with pebbles between fingers, for no game is caught with it, nor is an enemy harmed by it, but it breaks teeth and gouges out eyes. None narrated this hadith from Khuza'i ibn Ziyad except al-Haytham ibn al-Jahm."
"3635","3630 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Bishr al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn 'Amir, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj, from Nafi', he said: I was with Ibn 'Umar on a journey, and he hastened the march until the sun set; I called out to him: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the prayer! He went on until the stars intermingled, then dismounted and prayed Maghrib, and prayed 'Isha two rak'ahs, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when pressed by a matter used to pray like this. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj except 'Umar ibn 'Amir, nor did anyone narrate it from 'Umar except Salim ibn Nuh; Hilal ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"3636","3631 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning on a trunk; when the pulpit was made, the trunk moaned, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came down to it and embraced it, and it calmed. None narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Habban ibn Hilal; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan alone transmitted it."
"3637","3632 - Sahl ibn Abi Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Shadhan narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Muhammad Abu Hammam al-Kharaki narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: I heard Hammad say: Ibrahim informed me, that al-Aswad ibn Yazid narrated to him, that 'A'ishah informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter; and I forbade you from making nabidh in dubba, hantam and muzaffat vessels, so make nabidh in whatever you wish, but avoid every intoxicant. None narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Mansur ibn Sa'd; Abu Hammam al-Kharaki alone transmitted it."
"3638","3633 - Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, he said: al-Ruhayl ibn Mu'awiyah, the brother of Zuhayr, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to order a man to lead the Friday prayer with the people, then burn down the houses of people who stay away from it. None narrated this hadith from al-Ruhayl ibn Mu'awiyah except Ziyad al-Bakka'i; Ahmad ibn 'Abdah alone transmitted it."
"3639","3634 - Sahl ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Shadhan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Qaza'ah - of the people of Makkah, Kufan by origin - narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Abi 'A'ishah al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Mismar - meaning Muhajir, freedman of the family of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas - mention, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, that 'Ammar ibn Yasir said to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: Why do you not go out with 'Ali? Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will emerge a group from my ummah who will shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the target; 'Ali ibn Abi Talib will kill them - he said it three times. He said: Yes, by Allah, I heard it, but I preferred seclusion until I find a sword that cuts the disbeliever and spares the believer. This hadith is not narrated from 'Ammar ibn Yasir except with this chain; 'Isa ibn Shadhan alone transmitted it."
"3640","3635 - Salamah ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: My maternal grandfather Khattab ibn 'Uthman al-Fawzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi 'Ablah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying seated in supererogatory prayer until one or two years before his death; then I saw him praying seated in his supererogatory prayer, reciting the surah slowly until his recitation of it was longer than longer than it."
"3641","3636 - Salamah ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Khattab ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi 'Ablah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode a horse and fell from it, so his right side was scraped; one day he prayed for us one of the prayers while seated, so we prayed behind him seated. Then when he gave salam he said: The imam is appointed only to be followed: when the imam prays standing, pray standing; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise; and when he prays seated, pray seated all together."
"3642","3637 - Salamah ibn Ahmad al-Fawzi narrated to us, he said: My grandfather narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi 'Ablah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Abu 'Abd Allah al-Agharr, that Abu Hurayrah informed them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who comes early to the prayer, meaning Friday, is like one who offers a camel, then the one after him is like one who offers a cow, then the one after him is like one who offers a ram, then the one after him is like one who offers a chicken, then the one after him is like one who offers an egg."
"3643","3638 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn 'Adi, from 'Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque; a woman does not travel more than two days except with her husband or a mahram; two days in the year are not fasted: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha; and there is no prayer after two prayers: after Fajr until the sun rises, and after 'Asr until the sun sets."
"3644","3639 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, she said: I held the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said what I used to hear him say when visiting a sick person: Remove the affliction, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You. So he raised his head and said: Rather, O Allah, with the Highest Companion; rather, O Allah, with the Highest Companion."
"3645","3640 - Salamah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Which of you began the morning fasting? Abu Bakr said: I did. He said: Which of you visited a sick person? Abu Bakr said: I did. He said: Which of you followed a funeral? Abu Bakr said: I did. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings; whoever completes these, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. None narrated these hadiths from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except his son Yahya, and they are not narrated from his father except with this chain."
"3646","3641 - Salamah ibn Nahid al-Maqdisi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn 'Ulayy narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting; when he finished, he struck the ground with his palms and performed tayammum, then returned the greeting. None narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Maslamah ibn 'Ulayy; Hisham ibn 'Ammar alone transmitted it."
"3647","3642 - Salamah ibn Nahid narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn 'Ulayy narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not visit a sick person except after three days. None narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Maslamah ibn 'Ulayy; Hisham ibn 'Ammar alone transmitted it."
"3648","3643 - Salamah ibn Nahid narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Zurarah al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn al-Ashdaq narrated to me, from Kulayb ibn Hazn, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, seek Paradise with all your effort, and flee from the Fire with all your effort, for the seeker of Paradise does not sleep, and the fleer from the Fire does not sleep. Kulayb ibn Hazn did not attribute any hadith other than this one to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it is not narrated from him except with this chain."
"3649","3644 - Salamah ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Hani' al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Suhaym narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves from the Fire even with half a date. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb except Mubarak ibn Suhaym."
"3650","3645 - Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhalam al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Hurayth ibn Abi Matar, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touched me while he was fasting."
"3651","3646 - Sulayman ibn Ayyub ibn Hadhalam narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sa'dan ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Hurayth ibn Abi Matar, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad and 'Alqamah, from 'A'ishah, the like of it. None narrated this other hadith from Hurayth, from al-Hakam and Hammad, except Sa'dan ibn Yahya; Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"3652","3647 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Hakim ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, he said: I heard Umm Salamah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: After me there will be a swallowing of the earth in the east, a swallowing in the west, and a swallowing in the Arabian Peninsula. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will the earth swallow though among them are righteous people? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Yes, when most of its people are wicked. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Hakim ibn Nafi'."
"3653","3648 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Qasim ibn Ma'n narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has pardoned for my ummah what their souls whisper to them, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it. None narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Ma'n except al-Mu'afa ibn Sulayman."
"3654","3649 - Sulayman ibn al-Mu'afa narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: I used to hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, take my account with an easy reckoning. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the easy reckoning? He said: O 'A'ishah, He looks into his book and overlooks his evil deeds; as for whoever is interrogated closely in the reckoning, he is ruined. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn 'Urwah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Salamah alone transmitted it."
"3655","3650 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Marwan al-'Abdi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Makki, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Salimah, who is your chief today? They said: al-Jadd ibn Qays, but we consider him miserly. He said: And what disease is worse than miserliness? But your chief is 'Amr ibn al-Jamuh. None narrated this hadith from 'Amr ibn Dinar except Ibrahim ibn Yazid, nor from Ibrahim except Sulayman ibn Marwan; Suhayl ibn Ibrahim alone transmitted it."
"3656","3651 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord a question, and I wished I had not asked Him. I said: O Lord, there were messengers before me, among them one for whom You subjected the winds, and among them one who would revive the dead. He said: Did I not find you an orphan and shelter you? Did I not find you lost and guide you? Did I not expand your breast for you, and remove your burden from you? I said: Yes, O Lord. None raised this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani and Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri."
"3657","3652 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: 'Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to sit between two men except with their permission. None narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Ahmad ibn 'Abdah."
"3658","3653 - Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-'Attar narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father: that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin, and said to him: What wealth do you have? He said: Allah has given me of every kind of wealth. He said: When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see it upon him. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"3659","3654 - Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Yahya al-Tabib al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A surah of the Qur'an, which is only thirty verses, pleaded for its companion until it admitted him into Paradise, and it is Surah Tabarak."
"3660","3655 - Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tabib narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of these two foul-smelling greens, eating them and entering our mosques; if you must eat them, kill them thoroughly with fire. None narrated these two hadiths from Sallam ibn Miskin except Shayban ibn Farrukh."
"3661","3656 - Sulayman ibn Farakhi Abu al-Rabi' al-Farghani al-Misri narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever is made a judge has been slaughtered without a knife. None narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Bakr ibn Bakkar."
"3662","3657 - Sulayman ibn Farakhi al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: 'Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Ghubari narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man swearing by al-amanah (the trust), and said: Are you not the one who swears by al-amanah?! None narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd except 'Abd al-Warith; Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi alone transmitted it."
"3663","3658 - Salm ibn 'Isam Abu Umayyah al-Thaqafi al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Hafs ibn Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, steward of the family of al-Zubayr, from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No father has bequeathed his child anything better than good manners. None narrated this hadith from 'Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Musa, and it is not narrated from Ibn 'Umar except with this chain."
"3664","3659 - Salm ibn 'Isam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Hafs ibn Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, she said: I used to bathe with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a single vessel, saying: Leave some for me, leave some for me. None narrated this hadith from Yunus except Salim ibn Nuh; Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Hafs alone transmitted it."
"3665","3660 - Sayf ibn 'Amr Abu al-Tammam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-'Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Tariq Abu Qurrah narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Nujayd, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My ummah is like rain, it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end. Abu Nujayd is 'Imran ibn Husayn al-Khuza'i; this hadith is not narrated from 'Imran ibn Husayn except with this chain; Ibn Abi al-Sari alone transmitted it."
"3666","3661 - Sayf ibn 'Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-'Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Abu Hunaydah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water for ablution and performed ablution washing once each, then said: This is the ablution without which Allah does not accept prayer. Then he performed ablution washing twice each, and said: This is the ablution of the nations before you. Then he performed ablution washing three times each, and said: This is my ablution and the ablution of the prophets before me. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Buraydah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari alone transmitted it."
"3667","3662 - Sayf ibn 'Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn 'Abd Allah, from Sulayman ibn Abi Karimah, from Abu Qurrah 'Ata' ibn Abi Qurrah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Damrah al-Saluli, he said: I heard Abu al-Darda' say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he heard the call to prayer would say: O Allah, Lord of this perfect call and the established prayer, bless Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, and place us in his intercession on the Day of Resurrection. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says this at the call, Allah will place him in my intercession on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda' except with this chain; 'Amr ibn Abi Salamah alone transmitted it."
"3668","3663 - Shu'ayb ibn 'Imran al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: Idris al-Awdi narrated to me, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: al-Naqur is the Trumpet, and it is a horn. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I be at ease when it has been grasped. None narrated this hadith from Idris al-Awdi, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Abbas, except Ibn Abi Za'idah. And Abu Muslim, guide of al-A'mash, narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Idris, from 'Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"3669","3664 - Shu'ayb ibn 'Imran al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: Sa'd ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to me, from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the disbeliever: Who is your Lord? He will say: I do not know. At that moment he is deaf, blind and dumb; he will be struck with an iron hammer - if a mountain were struck with it, it would become dust - and everything will hear it except the two weighty beings. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, and Allah leaves the wrongdoers astray. None narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah."
"3670","3665 - Shu'ayb ibn 'Imran al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-'Askari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, he said: Rib'i ibn Hirash narrated to me, he said: While Hudhayfah and 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr Abu Mas'ud were sitting, one of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man from the Children of Israel used to dig up graves; he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then take my bones and grind them, then wait for a windy day and scatter me in it. That was done to him, and his Lord said to him: Why did you do that? He said: Out of fear of You, O Lord. So Allah forgave him. Then 'Uqbah said: And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it. None narrated this hadith from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah except his son Yahya."
"3671","3666 - Shabab ibn Salih al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from 'Anbasah al-Haddad, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Qur'an is disbelief. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except 'Anbasah al-Haddad."
"3672","3667 - Shabab ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm al-Bajali, from al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wine is the mother of evils; whoever drinks it, his prayer is not accepted for forty days, and if he dies with it in his belly, he dies the death of ignorance. None narrated this hadith from al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah except al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Rahman; Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah alone transmitted it."
"3673","3668 - Sharahil ibn al-'Ala' Abu al-Ward al-Balisi the judge narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Hisham al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Malik, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. None narrated this hadith from Malik except Ibn al-Mubarak; 'Ubayd ibn Hisham alone transmitted it."
"3674","3669 - Shayban ibn Muhammad Abu Ahmad al-Misma'i narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Wasi', from Ma'ruf, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three: fasting three days of every month, ghusl on Friday, and witr before sleeping."
"3675","3670 - Salih ibn Shu'ayb Abu Shu'ayb al-Basri, in Egypt, narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Rashid al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Qurayr narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar: that an aged old man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a deed by which I may draw near to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic. He said: Upon you is jihad in the path of Allah. He said: I cannot do that; I have grown old for that and weak. He said: Then be a muezzin. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Qurayr except Mubarak ibn Rashid; Dawud ibn Shabib alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Ibn 'Umar except with this chain."
"3676","3671 - Salih ibn Shu'ayb al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ammar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the adhan is called in a village, Allah secures it from His punishment that day. None narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd; Bakr ibn Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"3677","3672 - Salih ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and made to stand between Paradise and Hell; a caller will call: O people of Paradise, and they will look up. It will be said to them: Do you recognize this? They will say: O our Lord, this is death. Then it will be slaughtered between Paradise and Hell, and it will be said to them: Eternity, no death. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Khalid ibn Qays, nor from Khalid except Nuh ibn Qays; Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi alone transmitted it."
"3678","3673 - Salih ibn Muqatil ibn Salih al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Ghaffar al-Fuqaymi narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Juhayfah, from 'Ali, he said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet are Abu Bakr and 'Umar. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar except 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Ghaffar and his son 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar."
"3679","3674 - Salih narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-'Anbari narrated to us, from Harun ibn Ri'ab, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym al-'Adawi, from Qabisah ibn Mukhariq al-Hilali, he said: I undertook a hamilah (blood-money burden)... then he mentioned the hadith."
"3680","3675 - Salih ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Muqatil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Taymi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu 'Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not left after me a trial more harmful to men than women. None narrated this hadith from 'Asim al-Ahwal except Mindal; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Hamid alone transmitted it."
"3681","3676 - Salih ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Muqatil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce except after marriage. None narrated this hadith from Ayyub except 'Asim ibn Hilal; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i alone transmitted it."
"3682","3677 - Salih ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Muqatil narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Junadah ibn Salm narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from 'A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, I seek refuge in Your mercy from Your torment, and I seek refuge in You from You; I cannot enumerate praise of You, You are as You have praised Yourself. None narrated this hadith from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar except Junadah ibn Salm; Salm ibn Junadah alone transmitted it."
"3683","3678 - I heard Sulayhah bint Abi Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn say: I heard my father say: The Qur'an is the speech of Allah, uncreated; whoever says the Qur'an is created is a disbeliever."
"3684","3679 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: My brother Ishaq ibn 'Isa narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Uqbah, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Zuhri, from Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, from 'Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Withdrawal is not practiced from a free woman except with her permission. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, nor from Ja'far except Ibn Lahi'ah. Ishaq ibn 'Isa alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3685","3680 - Talib ibn Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man does not look at the nakedness of a man, nor does a woman look at the nakedness of a woman; a man does not lie with a man, nor does a woman lie with a woman. None narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman; Ibn Abi Fudayk and Zayd ibn al-Hubab alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain."
"3686","3681 - Talib ibn Qurrah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Tammam ibn Najih, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a westward expanse of Hell were placed in the middle of the earth, the stench of its wind and the severity of its heat would harm what is between the east and the west; and if a spark from the sparks of Hell were in the east, one in the west would feel its heat. None narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Tammam ibn Najih."
"3687","3682 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Isa al-Harbi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness. None narrated this hadith from Simak except Abu al-Ahwas; al-Hasan ibn 'Isa al-Harbi alone transmitted it."
"3688","3683 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Asim; then I met 'Asim in Makkah, and he narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever claims descent from other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him. Abu 'Uthman said: Then I met Abu Bakrah and mentioned that to him, and he said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). None narrated this hadith from Khalid, from 'Asim, except Ibn 'Ulayyah; Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' alone transmitted it."
"3689","3684 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not eat reclining. None included between 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar and Abu Juhayfah in this hadith 'Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah except Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba'. And a group narrated it from Abu 'Awanah, from Raqabah, from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah."
"3690","3685 - Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym Abu Salamah al-Kinani, from Yahya ibn Jabir al-Ta'i, from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seek refuge with Allah from greed that leads to avarice, and from greed that leads to what is not attainable."
"3691","3686 - Tahir ibn 'Ali al-Tabarani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Walid al-Tabarani narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn 'Adi narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Zumayl, from Abu Asma' al-Saksaki, from 'Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from 'Amr ibn Murrah except with this chain; al-Haytham ibn 'Adi alone transmitted it."
"3692","3687 - Tahir ibn 'Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bukayr al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The concubine of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Umm Ibrahim, was in a chamber of hers, and a Copt used to come to her bringing water and firewood; people said about that: a foreign man entering upon a foreign woman. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent 'Ali ibn Abi Talib and ordered him to kill him. He went and found him atop a palm tree; when the Copt saw the sword with 'Ali, he fell, throwing off the cloak that was on him, and leapt down - and he was castrated. So 'Ali returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if you order one of us with a command, then he sees otherwise - should he refer back to you? He said: Yes. So he informed him of what he had seen of the Copt. He said: Then Umm Ibrahim gave birth to Ibrahim, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in doubt about him until Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Peace be upon you, O father of Ibrahim. Then he was reassured of that. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yazid ibn Abi Habib and 'Uqayl ibn Khalid; Ibn Lahi'ah alone transmitted it from them."
"3693","3688 - Tahir ibn 'Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn 'Abbad al-Ru'asi narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ahmad ibn Abyad al-Madini narrated to me, from al-Awza'i, from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is adorned from year to year for the month of Ramadan, and the wide-eyed houris are adorned from year to year for the month of Ramadan. When the month of Ramadan enters, Paradise says: O Allah, place for us in this month dwellers from Your servants; and the wide-eyed houris say: O Allah, place for us in this month husbands from Your servants. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guards himself in the month of Ramadan - not drinking intoxicant in it, not accusing a believer of slander in it, and not committing a sin in it - Allah will marry him every night to a hundred houris, and build for him a palace in Paradise of gold, silver, ruby and peridot; if the world were gathered and placed in that palace, it would be in it only like a goat's tethering place in the world. And whoever drinks intoxicant in it, accuses a believer of slander in it, and commits a sin in it, Allah will nullify his deeds of a year. So beware of the month of Ramadan, for it is the month of Allah; if you are negligent in it, He has made eleven months for you in which you enjoy and delight, and made for Himself the month of Ramadan - so beware of the month of Ramadan. None narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Ahmad ibn Abyad al-Madini; Zuhayr ibn 'Abbad alone transmitted it."
"3694","3689 - Tahir ibn 'Isa ibn Qayras al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from his father and 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Salih, from Yazid, freedman of Salamah: that Umm Sulayman, his wife, asked 'A'ishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about the meat of the sacrifice. She said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib returned from a raid and entered upon Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and some sacrificial meat was brought near to him, but he refused to eat it until he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Eat it from Dhu al-Hijjah to Dhu al-Hijjah. Umm Sulayman, wife of Yazid ibn Abi 'Ubayd, freedman of Salamah ibn al-Akwa', narrated no hadith from 'A'ishah other than this; 'Amr ibn al-Harith alone transmitted it."
"3695","3690 - Tayy ibn Isma'il ibn al-Hasan ibn Qahtabah ibn Khalid ibn Ma'dan al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Mujahid, he said: A man came to al-Hasan and al-Husayn and asked them; they said: Begging is not proper except for three: for a crushing need, a burdensome surety burden, or a weighty debt. And they gave him. Then he came to Ibn 'Umar, who gave him without asking. The man said to him: I came to your cousins and they questioned me, while you did not question me? Ibn 'Umar said: The two sons of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were merely extracting knowledge thoroughly. None narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Yunus ibn Khabbab."
"3696","3691 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i, from Nafi' ibn 'Utbah, he said: Some Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to embrace Islam, wearing wool. I said: I will surely come between these people and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I said to myself: He is in private counsel with the people. Then my soul insisted I go to him, and I heard him say: You will conquer the Arabian Peninsula and Allah will open it; then you will conquer Persia and Allah will open it; then you will conquer the Dajjal and Allah will open him. None narrated this hadith from Musa ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr except 'Asim ibn 'Ali."
"3697","3692 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, he said: On the day of Khaybar the people suffered hunger, so they took the domestic donkeys and slaughtered them, and boiled the pots with them. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us, and we overturned the pots. And he said: Allah will bring you a provision more lawful for you than this and more wholesome than that. He said: So that day we overturned the pots while they were boiling. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, the flesh of horses and mules, every beast with fangs, every bird with talons, and forbade al-mujaththamah, al-khulsah and al-nuhbah. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar."
"3698","3693 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: My father 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu 'Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from his father Hudhayfah, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a beggar stood over us and the people were silent; then he returned and asked, and one of the people gave him a ring or something, so the people followed and gave him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever institutes a good practice and is followed in it, he has its reward and the like of the rewards of those who follow him in it, without diminishing anything from their rewards; and whoever adopts an evil practice and is followed in it, upon him is its burden and the like of the burdens of those who follow him in it, without diminishing anything from their burdens. None narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha' except 'Ali ibn 'Asim."
"3699","3694 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab Ja'far ibn al-Harith al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Razin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it three times, for he does not know where his hand spent the night. None narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ashhab except 'Ali ibn 'Asim."
"3700","3695 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrate from Anas ibn Malik: that he walked to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with rancid melted fat and barley bread, and he used to say: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, there did not remain in the household of Muhammad a sa' of wheat nor a sa' of dates - and they were then people of nine households. None narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except 'Asim ibn 'Ali."
"3701","3696 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn 'Ali, from his father, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas, he said: al-'Abbas sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I came to him in the evening while he was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood praying at night; when he had prayed the two rak'ahs before Fajr, he said: O Allah, I ask You for mercy from Yourself by which You guide my heart, gather my affairs, mend my disorder, restore my affection, rectify my religion, guard my absent, raise my present, purify my deeds, whiten my face, inspire me with my right guidance, and protect me from every evil. O Allah, grant me true faith and certainty after which there is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your nobility in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You success at the meeting, the abode of the martyrs, the life of the fortunate, the companionship of the prophets, and victory over the enemies. O Allah, I lay my need before You, though my judgment falls short, my deeds are weak, and I am in need of Your mercy; so I ask You, O Decider of matters and Healer of breasts, as You separate between the seas, to shelter me from the punishment of the Blaze, from the call of woe, and from the trial of the graves. O Allah, whatever good my judgment falls short of, my deeds are too weak for, and my intention or wish does not reach - of good You promised to any of Your servants or good You will give to any of Your creation - I desire it from You, and I ask You for it, O Lord of the Worlds. O Allah, make us guides, guided, neither straying nor misleading, at war with Your enemies and at peace with Your allies; we love people through love of You, and we oppose through enmity to You whoever of Your creation opposes You. O Allah, this is the supplication and upon You is the response; O Allah, this is the effort and upon You is reliance; there is no power nor strength except through Allah. O Allah, Possessor of the strong rope and the rightful command, I ask You for security on the Day of Threat, and Paradise on the Day of Eternity with the near ones, the witnesses, those who bow and prostrate, and those who fulfill covenants; You are Merciful, Loving, and You do what You will. Glory be to the One who donned might and spoke with it; glory be to the One to whom glorification is due; glory be to the Possessor of might and splendor; glory be to the Possessor of power and generosity; glory be to the One who encompassed everything with His knowledge. O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my grave, light in my hearing and light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in my bones, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, and light beneath me. O Allah, increase me in light, grant me light, and make light for me. None narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn 'Ali except Ibn Abi Layla."
"3702","3697 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send us out with no food except a advance portion of dates; we would divide it handful by handful, until we came to date by date. He said: I said: What use could date by date be to you? He said: Do not say that, for by Allah, no sooner did we lose them than we suffered hardship. None narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs except al-Mas'udi, and it is not narrated from 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah except with this chain."
"3703","3698 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Jahm al-Qurashi, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, he said: I came to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas for a need and saw him relieve himself and wipe over the khuffs. I said to him: Do you wipe over the khuffs? He said: Yes; when you meet your father, ask him. Ibn 'Umar said: So I met my father 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and asked him about that; he said: Yes; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did so, so we did so. None narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Jahm except Abu Bakr al-Nahshali and Abu Hanifah al-Nu'man ibn Thabit."
"3704","3699 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Shaybah al-Tamimi al-Basri narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not created a disease except that He has created for it a cure; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it - except al-sam, and it is death. None narrated this hadith from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Sa'id, except Shabib ibn Shaybah. And 'Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Husayn narrated it from 'Ata', from Abu Hurayrah. And Talhah ibn 'Amr al-Makki narrated it from 'Ata', from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3705","3700 - 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bilal al-Ash'ari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-'Ala' al-Razi narrated to us, from 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Farwah, from Qatan ibn Wahb, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Mus'ab ibn 'Umayr when he returned from Uhud, and stood over him and his companions, and said: I bear witness that you are alive with Allah; so visit them and greet them, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, none greets them except that they return it until the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn 'Umar except with this chain; Abu Bilal alone transmitted it."
"3706","3701 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Umar al-Darir narrated to us, he said: 'Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah created the Garden of Eden and built it with His Hand: a brick of gold and a brick of silver, made its mortar musk, its soil saffron, its pebbles pearls; then He said to it: Speak. It said: The believers have succeeded. The angels said: Blessed are you, abode of kings. None narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except 'Adi ibn al-Fadl."
"3707","3702 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar al-Qati'i narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr al-Awza'i narrated to me, that Ya'ish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham narrated to him, he said: Ma'dan ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me, from Abu al-Darda': that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke his fast? Then I met Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Abu al-Darda' said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vomited and broke his fast? He said: And I poured water for him and he performed ablution. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except al-Husayn."
"3708","3703 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' al-Ghudani narrated to us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Shabib ibn Gharqadah, from Abu Maytha' al-Mustazill ibn Husayn, he said: I heard Jarir ibn 'Abd Allah - and he was our governor - say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I went back, so he called me and said: I will not accept from you until you pledge, and sincere counsel for every Muslim. So I pledged to him. None narrated this hadith from Shabib ibn Gharqadah except Isra'il; 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' alone transmitted it."
"3709","3704 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Every prayer in which the Mother of the Qur'an is not recited is deficient, deficient, deficient. None narrated this hadith from 'Asim except Aban; Sa'id ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"3710","3705 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Hajib ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: They are those who do not seek ruqyah, do not cauterize, do not take omens, and rely upon their Lord. He said: Affliction kept befalling us until we cauterized, but we neither prospered nor succeeded. None narrated this hadith from al-Hakam ibn al-A'raj except Hajib ibn 'Umar, and he is Abu Khushaynah."
"3711","3706 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Nothing is more noble to Allah than supplication. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except 'Imran al-Qattan."
"3712","3707 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man remains in prayer so long as he is in the place where he prayed, so long as he does not break his ablution. None narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muzani except 'Imran al-Qattan."
"3713","3708 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, he said: 'Umar ibn Farrukh, keeper of the saddle-bags, narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it is edible, wool on the back, and milk in the udder. None narrated this hadith from Habib ibn al-Zubayr except 'Umar ibn Farrukh, and this wording - nor wool on the back, nor milk in the udder - is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3714","3709 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Rashid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, Zakariyya, Isma'il and Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad and 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Warrad, he said: Mu'awiyah wrote to al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So al-Mughirah wrote to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when finishing the prayer: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things Powerful. O Allah, none withholds what You give, none gives what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail against You. And he used to forbid gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth. None narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Hushaym; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali alone transmitted it."
"3715","3710 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Abd Allah al-Shami narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Asbat narrated to us, from Muhill ibn Khalifah al-Dabbi, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from 'Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is discontent with his provision, spreads his complaints, and does not persevere, no deed of his ascends to Allah, and he meets Allah while He is angry with him. None narrated this hadith from Ibrahim except Muhill, nor from Muhill except Yusuf ibn Asbat; 'Uthman ibn 'Abd Allah al-Shami alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3716","3711 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Isma'il."
"3717","3712 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn 'Utaybah narrated to us, from al-Bahiyy, freedman of al-Zubayr, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Throw the khumrah mat for me in the mosque. I said: I am menstruating. He said: Your menstruation is not in your hand; throw it to me. She said: So I threw it to him, and he prayed upon it. None narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Ibrahim."
"3718","3713 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; what is beyond that is charity. None narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Aban."
"3719","3714 - 'Uthman ibn 'Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes an image will be burdened on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it; whoever listens to the speech of people who dislike him, molten lead will be poured into his ears; and whoever pretends a false dream will be burdened to tie between two barley grains. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Talhah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman."
"3720","3715 - 'Uthman ibn 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Uthman ibn Zufar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Zuhri al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tanning the hide is its purification. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Muhammad ibn Muslim; al-Haytham ibn Jamil alone transmitted it."
"3721","3716 - 'Uthman ibn al-Hasan al-Hunayni the judge narrated to us, he said: al-Musayyab ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the frog, and said: Its croaking is glorification. None raised this hadith from Shu'bah except Hajjaj; al-Musayyab ibn Wadih alone transmitted it."
"3722","3717 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Sulafi al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent 'Uthman ibn 'Affan to Abu Bakr asking him for their inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 'A'ishah said: I was the one who turned them back from that; I sent to them: Do not do so; did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. So they returned."
"3723","3718 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Sulafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: Fatimah spoke to Abu Bakr about her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Does your daughter inherit you, while I do not inherit my father? He said: May my father be ransom for you and for your father; he used to say: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. None narrated these two hadiths from Ja'far ibn al-Harith - and he is Abu al-Ashhab al-Nakha'i al-Kufi - except Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash."
"3724","3719 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Sulafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' al-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him not put anything in it until he washes it seven times. None narrated it from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad; Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash alone transmitted it."
"3725","3720 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Sulafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two traders differ about the sale while the commodity stands intact as it is, not consumed, the word is what the seller says, or they annul the sale. None narrated this hadith from Musa ibn 'Uqbah except Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash."
"3726","3721 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr al-Sulafi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Shaybah al-Rahawi, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu 'Ubaydah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him. None narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Abu Shaybah; Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash alone transmitted it."
"3727","3722 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Utbah ibn Humayd, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: We have no evil example; the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."
"3728","3723 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us istikhara in matters as he would teach one of us a surah of the Qur'an: O Allah, I seek good from You by Your knowledge, seek power from You by Your power, and ask You of Your bounty; for You decree and I do not decree, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if there is good in this matter for my religion, my world and the outcome of my affair, decree it for me; and if other than that is better for me, make good easy for me wherever it is, turn evil away from me, and make me content with Your decree. None narrated this hadith from Abu Hanifah except Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash."
"3729","3724 - 'Uthman ibn Khalid ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Mas'udi, from Hammad and al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it about istikhara. None narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except al-Mas'udi."
"3730","3725 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs in Madinah. Then Ibn Umm Maktum came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind. So he permitted him for some days, then he ordered his dog and it was killed."
"3731","3726 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir, he said: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am blind, my house is far, and I hear the adhan. He said: If you hear the adhan, then come, even crawling."
"3732","3727 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that wine has been forbidden? He said: Yes. He said: I have wine belonging to an orphan. So he ordered it and it was poured out."
"3733","3728 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to me, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir, he said: Ibn Mas'ud entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing delivering the sermon; he sat beside Ubayy and asked about something, but he did not answer him. When he finished his prayer, Ibn Mas'ud said to Ubayy: What prevented you from replying to me? He said: You did not attend Friday prayer with us. He said: Why? He said: Because you spoke while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ubayy spoke the truth."
"3734","3729 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir, he said: A Muslim man was standing upon a rock praying in Makkah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not tire until you tire."
"3735","3730 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, the grandsons of the Ansar, their wives, and their offspring."
"3736","3731 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir, he said: Ubayy came and said: O Messenger of Allah, something happened from me tonight: some women gathered in my house who do not recite, so I led them in eight rak'ahs, then prayed witr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, as if in approval."
"3737","3732 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you lead prayer, shorten it, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, the sick, and the one with a need."
"3738","3733 - 'Uthman ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Talhi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub al-Qummi narrated to us, from 'Isa ibn Jariyah, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer in the month of Ramadan, eight rak'ahs, and prayed witr. When the next year came, we gathered in the mosque hoping he would lead us. He said: I feared - or disliked - that it be made obligatory upon you."
"3739","3734 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' al-Ghudani narrated to us, he said: 'Imran al-Qattan informed us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah: that he met Abu Dharr at al-Rabadhah, driving a camel of his with two water-skins on it and a water-skin on the camel's neck. I said: O Abu Dharr, what is the matter with you? He said: My deeds are my own. I said: Narrate to me, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No two Muslims between whom three children die before reaching puberty, except that they are forgiven by virtue of His mercy to them. I said: Tell me more, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever spends two pairs of his wealth in the path of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will all receive him, each calling him to what is with him. I said: Two pairs of what? He said: Whoever owns horses, two horses; whoever owns camels, two camels; whoever owns cattle, two cows - until he listed kinds of this sort. None narrated this hadith from 'Imran al-Qattan except 'Abd Allah ibn Raja'."
"3740","3735 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: 'Isa ibn Dinar the muezzin, freedman of 'Amr ibn al-Harith al-Khuza'i, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from 'Amr ibn al-Harith: that he heard 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud say: I did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more often than I fasted thirty days with him. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud except with this chain; 'Isa ibn Dinar alone transmitted it."
"3741","3736 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Rabi'ah al-Kinani narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh: that he heard 'Ali, when asked about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he poured water in the courtyard, then said: Where is the questioner about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then he washed his hands three times, his face three times, his forearms three times, wiped his head until it was about to drip, and washed his feet three times each. Then he said: Such was the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). None narrated this hadith from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr except Rabi'ah al-Kinani - and he is Rabi'ah ibn 'Ubayd, a Kufan - and Abu Maryam 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim al-Ansari."
"3742","3737 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abi al-Hurr al-Kindi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while we were sitting, and said: No morning has ever come upon me except that I sought Allah's forgiveness in it a hundred times. None narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah except al-Mughirah ibn Abi al-Hurr."
"3743","3738 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Fatimah bint 'Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, she said: My father said, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever frees a Muslim or believing soul, Allah will shield every limb of him with a limb of it from the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from 'Ali except with this chain; al-Hakam ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm alone transmitted it."
"3744","3739 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Umayyah al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not display gloating over your brother, lest Allah relieve him and afflict you. None narrated this hadith from Makhul except Burd, nor from Burd except Hafs, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3745","3740 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' narrated to us, he said: 'Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa': that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Scrolls of Ibrahim were revealed on the first night of Ramadan; the Torah was revealed on the sixth of Ramadan past; the Gospel was revealed on the thirteenth of Ramadan past; the Psalms were revealed on the eighteenth of Ramadan elapsed; and the Qur'an was revealed on the twenty-fourth of Ramadan elapsed. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except 'Imran al-Qattan, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3746","3741 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Sarjis narrated to me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to bathe with the leftover of a woman, or a woman with the leftover of a man, but they draw together. None narrated this hadith from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from 'Abd Allah ibn Sarjis, except 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar; Mu'alla ibn Asad alone transmitted it. And others narrated it from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Sawadah ibn 'Amr, from al-Hakam ibn 'Amr al-Ghifari."
"3747","3742 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Maymun, muezzin of the mosque of al-Ramlah, narrated to us, he said: 'Urwah ibn Ruwaym narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Qurt: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he was taken to al-Aqsa Mosque - when he returned he was between the Maqam and Zamzam, with Jibril on his right and Mika'il on his left - they flew with him until he reached the seven heavens. When he returned he said: I heard glorification in the highest heavens along with much glorification; the highest heavens glorified, out of awe of the Possessor of Majesty, fearful before the Possessor of Loftiness for His exaltedness: Glory be to the Most High, the Highest; glory be to Him, exalted is He. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Sa'id ibn Mansur alone transmitted it."
"3748","3743 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Nadlah ibn Sakan al-Maliki narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his grandfather, my mother's father, Nuqadah al-Asadi, he said: He sent a milch camel with me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to me: Milk it. So I milked it. He said: O Nuqadah, leave the caller of the milk. So I left its teats standing, not draining all the milk. This hadith is not narrated from Nuqadah except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi alone transmitted it."
"3749","3744 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Shaddad ibn Sa'id al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn 'Amr al-Rasibi narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people gather in a sitting then disperse without remembering Allah, except that sitting will be a regret upon them on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal except with this chain; Shaddad ibn Sa'id alone transmitted it."
"3750","3745 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. This hadith is not narrated from Bilal ibn al-Harith except with this chain; al-Qa'nabi alone transmitted it."
"3751","3746 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Rabi'ah Fahd ibn 'Awf narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Musa informed me, he said: 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar informed us, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: I ate a tharid of wheat bread with fatty meat, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) belching. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Restrain your belching from us, for those most satiated in this world will be hungriest in the Hereafter. None narrated this hadith from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar except 'Ali ibn Musa; Fahd ibn 'Awf alone transmitted it."
"3752","3747 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: Bahr ibn Mirar narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, he said: Abu Bakrah narrated, he said: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was walking between me and another man, he came upon two graves and said: The occupants of these two graves are being punished; bring me a palm stalk. Abu Bakrah said: My companion and I raced, and I brought him a stalk; he split it in two, placing one in this grave and one in that grave. He said: Perhaps it will be lightened for them so long as they remain moist. They are being punished for no great matter: backbiting and urine. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except from the hadith of al-Aswad ibn Shayban, and none rendered it soundly from al-Aswad ibn Shayban except Muslim ibn Ibrahim. And Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from al-Aswad ibn Shayban, from Bahr ibn Mirar, from Abu Bakrah."
"3753","3748 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Rabi'ah Fahd ibn 'Awf narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu al-Juwayriyah al-Jarmi, he said: We were in the land of the Romans, when a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), of Banu Sulaym, called Ma'n ibn Yazid al-Sulami, passed us. He said: I found a red jar containing dinars, and brought it to him; he took the fifth from it and said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no nafal except after the fifth, I would have given it to you. He said: Then he offered me from his share, and I said: I have no need of it. This hadith is not narrated from Ma'n ibn Yazid except with this chain; Abu 'Awanah alone transmitted it."
"3754","3749 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ziyad ibn 'Ilaqah, from 'Arfajah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be troubles and troubles; whoever you see walking to the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to divide their unity, kill him. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar except Hammad ibn Zayd; 'Arim alone transmitted it."
"3755","3750 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ata' ibn Yazid, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring on his hand and began tapping it with a stick he had. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was inattentive, he threw it away. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I think we have pained you and cost you. None narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, and it is not narrated from Abu Tha'labah except with this chain."
"3756","3751 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Bahr Abu Salamah al-'Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day felt pain and sent for 'Uthman. She said: I heard him say: Allah will clothe you with a shirt; if they want you to take it off, do not take it off. It was said to her: Where were you, why did you not mention this? She said: I forgot it. None narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn 'Urwah except Hammad ibn Salamah; al-Minhal ibn Bahr alone transmitted it."
"3757","3752 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan does not take my likeness. None narrated this hadith from Thabit except 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"3758","3753 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj, from Nafi', from Zayd ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who drinks in a silver vessel only gulps the Fire of Hell in his belly. None narrated this hadith from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj except Hammad ibn Zayd; 'Arim alone transmitted it."
"3759","3754 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Umm 'Urwah bint Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from her father, from her grandmother Safiyyah bint 'Abd al-Muttalib: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Uhud, he placed his women in a fort called Fari', and placed Hassan ibn Thabit with them. Hassan would look out toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when it pressed hard upon the polytheists he pressed along with him while in the fort, and when he returned he returned behind him. Some Jews came; one of them climbed the fort until he looked down upon us. I said to Hassan: Get up to him and kill him. He said: That is not in me; had that been in me, I would have been with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Safiyyah said: So I struck his head until I severed it. When I had severed it, I said: O Hassan, get up to his head and throw it at them while they are below the fort. He said: By Allah, that is not in me. She said: So I took his head and threw it at them. They said: By Allah, we knew Muhammad would not leave his family behind without anyone with them. And they dispersed. She said: Sa'd ibn Mu'adh passed by us, with a yellowness as if he had been a bridegroom shortly before, chanting rajaz. This hadith is not narrated from Safiyyah except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi alone transmitted it."
"3760","3755 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf al-'Ammi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah, from Umm 'Atiyyah, from her sister Duba'ah: that she saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat a shoulder, then stand for prayer without performing ablution. None narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Musa ibn Khalaf; his son Khalaf ibn Musa alone transmitted it. And Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah from whom Qatadah narrated this hadith is Ishaq ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, and Duba'ah is bint al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib."
"3761","3756 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il al-Nahdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would join fasts from suhur to suhur. None narrated this hadith from Ibn 'Aqil except Sharik, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"3762","3757 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Take suhur even with something. None narrated this hadith from Ibn 'Aqil except Sharik, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"3763","3758 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: 'Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Mas'ud al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: Umm Kulthum bint Thumamah al-Habati narrated to me, that her brother al-Mukhariq ibn Thumamah al-Habati said to her: Enter upon the Mother of the Believers 'A'ishah and convey my salam to her. So I entered upon her and said: One of your sons conveys salam to you. She said: Upon him and the mercy of Allah. I said: And he asks you to narrate to him about 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, for people have said much about him among us since he was killed. She said: As for me, I bear witness that 'Uthman ibn 'Affan was in this house, with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Jibril was revealing - he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a hot night, and when revelation descended upon him a heaviness descended upon him; Allah, Majestic is His mention, says: We shall cast upon you a weighty word - and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was striking the shoulder of 'Uthman, saying: Write, O 'Uthman. Allah would not bring down that station from His Prophet except upon a noble man. Whoever curses 'Uthman, upon him is the curse of Allah. None narrated this hadith from Umm Kulthum bint Thumamah except Hammad ibn Ibrahim al-Yashkuri."
"3764","3759 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Shuja' al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Warqa' bint Haddab narrated to me, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, when he left his house, would pass by the Mothers of the Believers, greeting them before coming to his assembly; when he returned to his house he would pass by them. Each time he passed he found a man sitting at the door of 'A'ishah. He said to him: Why do I see you sitting here? He said: I have a due I seek from the Mother of the Believers. So 'Umar entered upon her and said to her: O Mother of the Believers, is seven thousand each year not sufficient for you? She said: Yes, but I have obligations in it; I heard Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever owes a debt and is concerned to repay it, or intends to repay it, there remains with him a guard from Allah. So I love that there remains with me a guard from Allah. None narrated this hadith from Warqa' bint Haddab except Talhah ibn Shuja', and he is a Basran shaykh; Muslim ibn Ibrahim alone transmitted it."
"3765","3760 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of one who testifies that there is no god but Allah is not lawful except by one of three: a married person who commits adultery after chastity; a man who deliberately kills a believer, so he is killed for him; and a man who goes out warring against Allah and His Messenger, so he is killed and crucified, or exiled from the land. None narrated this hadith from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr except 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay'; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone transmitted it."
"3766","3761 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I entered upon 'A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, and with her was a slave-girl of hers wearing a cotton shirt worth five dirhams. She said: Raise your head to my slave-girl; look at her, for she prides herself on wearing it in the house, though I once had such a shirt in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no woman adorned in Madinah but sent to me to borrow it."
"3767","3762 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I entered upon 'A'ishah and asked her about two rak'ahs after 'Asr. She said: By the One who took his soul (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he never left them until he met Allah, and he did not meet Allah until he had grown heavy for prayer, praying much of his prayer seated. Umm Ayman said to her: 'Uthman used to forbid them? She said: You spoke the truth, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray them, though he would not pray them in the mosque fearing to burden his ummah, and he loved what was light for them."
"3768","3763 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I entered upon 'A'ishah, and 'A'ishah said: I entered upon Barirah while she was a mukatabah. She said: Buy me and free me. I said: Yes. Barirah said: My family will not sell me until they stipulate my wala'. 'A'ishah said: I have no need of that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard of that and mentioned it to 'A'ishah; 'A'ishah mentioned what they said. He said: Buy her and free her, and let them stipulate whatever they wish. So 'A'ishah bought her, and her family stipulated the wala'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala' belongs to whoever frees, even if they stipulate a hundred conditions. None narrated these hadiths from 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman except Abu Nu'aym."
"3769","3764 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us, he said: Muti' ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah bint 'Ismah narrated to us, from the Mother of the Believers 'A'ishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Do women go out on Eid? He said: Yes. It was said: The secluded maiden? He said: Yes; if she has no garment to wear, let her wear her companion's garment. This hadith is not narrated from 'A'ishah except with this chain; Muti' ibn Maymun alone transmitted it."
"3770","3765 - 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-'Ammi narrated to us, he said: Muti' ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Safiyyah bint 'Ismah narrated to us, from 'A'ishah: that a woman extended her hand to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he withheld his hand. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I extended my hand to you with a book, but you did not take it? He said: I do not know whether it is a woman's hand or a man's hand? I said: Rather a woman's hand. He said: If you were a woman, you would have changed your nails with henna. This hadith is not narrated from 'A'ishah except with this chain; Muti' ibn Maymun alone transmitted it."
"3771","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub al-Ansari narrated to me, from his father who said: I heard my uncle Mujammi' ibn Jariyah say: We returned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from al-Hudaybiyah until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Kura' al-Ghamim, when the people began hurrying toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some people said to others: What is wrong with the people? They said: Revelation has come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So we went out until we found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing at Kura' al-Ghamim, and when the people gathered he recited to them: {Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory}. Someone said to him: O Messenger of Allah, is it a victory? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, indeed it is a victory. This hadith is not narrated from Mujammi' ibn Jariyah except with this chain; Mujammi' ibn Ya'qub was alone in transmitting it."
"3772","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Zufar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ardak narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Walibah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour will not come until obscenity and miserliness appear, the trustworthy is deemed treacherous and the treacherous is trusted, the wu'ul perish and the tuhut appear. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the wu'ul and what are the tuhut? He said: The wu'ul are the prominent people and their nobles, and the tuhut are those who were beneath people's feet and unknown. This hadith is not narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr except with this chain; Ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"3773","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani narrated to me, from Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I saw some Arab men come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say: O Messenger of Allah, we own livestock and we pay its charity; will that suffice us instead of the Ramadan zakah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; pay it on behalf of the young and the old, the free and the slave, for it is a purification for you. No one narrated this hadith from Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman except Kathir ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani."
"3774","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Hakim and Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Religion is sincere advice, religion is sincere advice - three times. They said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims and their common folk. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam except Ibn Ajlan, and no one narrated it from Ibn Ajlan except Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"3775","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam, from his father, from his grandfather, from Kathir ibn Jurayj, that he heard Umm Dharrah report that A'ishah told her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Sit until Jibril comes to me so you may greet him and he supplicates good for you. Then Jibril came and stood at the door, then turned back and did not enter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with Jibril that he turned back and did not enter? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him another time and said: O Jibril, A'ishah sat to greet you and for you to supplicate good for her, yet you turned back from our door and did not enter upon us? Jibril said: I came to enter upon you but I found that foul little creature in your house, and we do not enter a house in which there is that creature or images. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Dharrah except with this chain; Ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"3776","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ghanim ibn al-Ahwas, that he heard Abu Salih al-Samman say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows, and no servant joins a row except that Allah raises him a degree by it and the angels shower goodness upon him. Ghanim ibn al-Ahwas did not narrate from Abu Salih any hadith other than this one; Ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"3777","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah ibn Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who asks Allah except that Allah gives him what he asked or averts from him an equal amount of evil, so long as he does not supplicate for sin or severing kinship. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Abd Allah except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"3778","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the market and saw heaped food; he put his hand into it and brought out moist food that rain had reached. He said to its owner: What made you do this? He said: By the One Who sent you with the truth, it is but one food. He said: Why did you not separate the moist apart and the dry apart, so buyers buy knowingly? Whoever cheats us is not of us. This hadith is not narrated from Anas ibn Malik except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"3779","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Aslam who said: I went out on a journey, and when I returned Umar said to me: Whom did you accompany? I said: I accompanied a man from Banu Bakr ibn Wa'il. Umar said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Your Bakri brother - yet do not trust him. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"3780","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn al-Harith ibn Rafi' ibn Makith al-Juhani narrated to me, from his father al-Harith, that he asked Jabir ibn Abd Allah, saying: We have sheep and young servants at Tharir, and they beat down for their sheep this hubalah fruit - Kharijah said, it is the fruit of the samar tree. Jabir said: No, then said: The sanctuary of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is neither beaten nor cut, but shake gently. Then Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid cutting the masad - Kharijah said, the masad is the pulley-strap of the bucket. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Kharijah ibn al-Harith was alone in transmitting it."
"3781","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to me: Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to me, from Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from Awf ibn al-Harith ibn al-Tufayl, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O A'ishah, beware of belittled sins, for they have a seeker from Allah. This hadith is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain; Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak was alone in transmitting it."
"3782","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no harm nor reciprocating harm; a man may place his timber upon his neighbor's wall; and when you doubt about the road, make it seven cubits. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Ma'mar."
"3783","Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashja'i narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Shaybah al-Ta'ifi narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: O people, O company of those who believed with their tongues while faith has not sincerely reached their hearts - until the secluded maidens in their chambers heard - do not harm the Muslims and do not pursue their faults, for whoever pursues his brother's fault, Allah will pursue his fault until He exposes him in the midst of his house. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Isma'il ibn Shaybah; Qudamah ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"3784","Ali ibn Bishr ibn Hilal al-Maqaridi al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih al-Makki, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Fear Allah wherever you are, and deal with people with good character. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Salih except Sa'id ibn Salim; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti was alone in transmitting it."
"3785","Ali ibn Bishr al-Maqaridi al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people ever sit in a house of the houses of Allah reciting the Book of Allah and studying it among themselves except that mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, the angels surround them, Allah mentions them among those with Him; and whoever travels a path seeking knowledge, Allah eases thereby a path to Paradise for him; and whoever is slowed by his deeds, his lineage will not hasten him. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Salih except Sa'id ibn Salim; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti was alone in transmitting it."
"3786","Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Sufi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Qudamah ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Abadah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from al-Sabbi ibn Ma'bad, that he entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together, and mentioned that to Umar, who said: You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Burd ibn Sinan except Qudamah ibn Shihab. Burd ibn Sinan differed with Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, for Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Amir, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Dabbi; so if Burd preserved it, it is unfamiliar from Zirr."
"3787","Ali ibn Siraj al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Muslim al-Najjar al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Khulayd ibn Da'laj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing the servant will be asked about on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer; it will be examined - if it is sound he has succeeded, and if it is corrupt he has failed and lost. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah from Anas except Khulayd ibn Da'laj; Rawh ibn Abd al-Wahid was alone in transmitting it."
"3788","Ali ibn Siraj al-Misri narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Muslim al-Najjar narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Umarah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed the people at al-Jabiyah and said: O people, whoever wishes to ask about the Qur'an, let him come to Ubayy ibn Ka'b; whoever wishes to ask about inheritance laws, let him come to Zayd ibn Thabit; whoever wishes to ask about understanding of religion, let him come to Mu'adh ibn Jabal; and whoever wishes to ask about wealth, let him come to me, for Allah has made me its guardian and distributor. I begin with the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the first Emigrants {who were expelled from their homes and wealth} - he recited the whole verse - whoever hastened to emigration, the grant hastens to him, and whoever lagged in emigration, the grant lags for him; so let no man blame but the resting place of his camel. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn al-Husayn except his son Sulayman; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad Umarah al-Ansari was alone in transmitting it."
"3789","Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Shaybah, from Abu Habib ibn Ya'la ibn Munabbih, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: The hyena has devoured us - Mis'ar said, meaning the year of drought. Umar asked him: From whom are you? He kept tracing his lineage until he knew him, and behold he was wealthy. Umar said: If a man had one valley or two valleys he would seek a third besides them. Ibn Abbas said: And nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, then Allah turns thereafter to whoever repents. Umar said to Ibn Abbas: From whom did you hear this? He said: From Ubayy ibn Ka'b. He said: When morning comes, come to me in the morning. So he went in the morning to his mother Umm al-Fadl and mentioned that to her; she said: What is with you and speaking in Umar's presence? Ibn Abbas feared that Ubayy had forgotten, so his mother said to him: Ubayy may well not have forgotten. So he went in the morning to Umar with the stick, and they set out to Ubayy; he came out to them having performed ablution and said: I was afflicted by madhiy, so I washed my private part - Mis'ar doubted - Umar said: Does that suffice? He said: Yes. He said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. And he asked him about what Ibn Abbas had said, and he confirmed him. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Muhammad ibn Bishr."
"3790","Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to me, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no judge who judges between people except that he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with an angel holding his nape until he makes him stand over Hell, then he raises his head to the heaven; if Allah, Majestic is His remembrance, says: Throw him, he will fall forty autumns. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Mas'ud except Masruq, nor from Masruq except al-Sha'bi, nor from al-Sha'bi except Mujalid; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan was alone in transmitting it."
"3791","Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave drink, he said: Begin with the elder, or with the elders. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha' except Ibn al-Mubarak, and no one narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak except al-Walid ibn Muslim and Ibn Sahm."
"3792","Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn A'ishah al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Amr, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek your needs from those with beautiful faces. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayrah except Ata, nor from Ata except Talhah, nor from Talhah except Safwan ibn Isa; Ibn A'ishah was alone in transmitting it."
"3793","Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yusuf al-Zimmi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed adultery while she was pregnant, so he delayed her by a year until she gave birth, then he ordered that her clothes be tied upon her, then ordered her stoning, then prayed over her. A man said to him: Do you pray over her though she committed adultery and you stoned her? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She has repented a repentance which, had seventy of the people of Madinah repented it, it would have been accepted from them; have you found anything better than that she gave herself up? No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi."
"3794","Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Salih al-Sa'igh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi the judge narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender of hearts. Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Yahya al-Qattan; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi was alone in transmitting it."
"3795","Ali ibn Bayan al-Mutarriz al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar Salih ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Did you witness the Pledge of al-Ridwan with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. I said: What was he wearing? He said: A cotton shirt, a stuffed cloak, a sheet, and a sword; and I saw al-Nu'man ibn Muqarrin al-Muzani standing over his head, lifting the branches of the tree from over his head, while the people were pledging him. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi; Salih ibn Harb was alone in transmitting it."
"3796","Ali ibn Bayan al-Mutarriz narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bashshar al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Hammad Abu al-Harith al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ulayyah, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked every fanged beast of prey and every clawed bird. No one narrated this hadith from Shu'bah except Abu al-Harith al-Warraq; Ahmad ibn Bashshar was alone in transmitting it."
"3797","Ali ibn Bayan al-Mutarriz narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'mar Salih ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to pray at night, little or much, and to make that witr."
"3798","Ali ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit who said: Anas ibn Malik mentioned seventy of the Ansar; he said: When night covered them they would shelter with a teacher in Madinah and spend the night with him studying the Qur'an; in the morning, whoever had strength would gather firewood and fetch sweet water, and whoever had means would get a sheep and prepare it, and it would end up hanging by the apartments of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When Khubayb was struck, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them; among them was my uncle Haram ibn Milhan. They came upon a clan of Banu Sulaym; Haram said to their leader: Shall I inform these people that we do not seek them, so they let us pass? He said: Yes. So he went to them and told them that, but a man among them met him with a spear and pierced him through. When Haram felt the spear in his belly he said: Allah is Most Great, I have won by the Lord of the Ka'bah. Then they closed in on them, and none of them remained to report. He said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieve over an expedition as he grieved over them. Anas said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he prayed the dawn prayer raise his hands supplicating against them. After that Abu Talhah came saying to me: Do you want the killer of Haram? I said: What is his state? May Allah do to him and do. Abu Talhah said: Do not do so, for he has embraced Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah except Affan."
"3799","Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Tamim ibn Zayd ibn Halah ibn Abi Halah al-Tamimi narrated to us in Egypt, he said: My father Muhammad narrated to me, from his father Amr ibn Tamim, from his father Tamim, from his father Zayd ibn Halah, from his father Halah, that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was asleep; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke and drew Halah to his chest, saying: Halah, Halah, Halah. Abu al-Qasim said: It is as if he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced in him because of his kinship to Khadijah. We did not write this hadith except from this shaykh."
"3800","Ali ibn Sa'id ibn Bashir al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Khazzaz al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Sa'dad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh who said: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b: Ibn Umm Abd said: Whoever stands the whole year will attain Laylat al-Qadr. Ubayy said: By Allah, it is in Ramadan, and it is the night of the twenty-seventh; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us, and its sign is that the sun rises having no rays. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except Sa'dad ibn Sulayman; Hasan ibn Husayn al-Ansari was alone in transmitting it."
"3801","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Khazzaz narrated to me, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: Sa'dad ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Ja'd the freedman of Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah who said: We met Ali wearing two garments in winter, and we said to him: Do not be deceived by this land of ours, for this land of ours is intensely cold, unlike your land. He said: I used to feel cold, but when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Khaybar I said: I have ophthalmia; so he spat in my eyes, and since then I have felt neither cold nor heat, and my eyes never ached. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except Sa'dad ibn Sulayman; Hasan ibn Husayn was alone in transmitting it. There is disagreement over the name of Sa'dad ibn Sulayman: some say Sa'dad and some say Mas'ud."
"3802","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Musa ibn al-Musayyab, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent al-Walid ibn Uqbah to Banu Wali'ah, between whom there was hatred in the pre-Islamic era. When he reached Banu Wali'ah they came out to meet him to see what was in his heart, so he feared the people and returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Banu Wali'ah wanted to kill me and withheld charity. When the report of what al-Walid had said before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Banu Wali'ah, they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Walid has lied; rather there was hatred between us and him, and we feared he would punish us for what was between us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Banu Wali'ah shall desist, or I shall send to them a man who is to me as myself, who will kill their fighters and take their offspring captive - and he is this one. Then he struck with his hand upon the shoulder of Ali ibn Abi Talib. And Allah revealed concerning al-Walid: {O you who believe, if a corrupt one comes to you} - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Quddus."
"3803","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Abi Saghirah al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from his father, from al-Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is as if a rider has come to you and alighted among you, saying: The land is our land and the city is our city; you are but our slaves and hirelings - separating widows and orphans from what Allah bestowed upon their forefathers. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri except Anbasah ibn Abi Saghirah; Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Mawsili was alone in transmitting it."
"3804","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to me, he said: My uncle Ubayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Zubayd, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ali, Fatimah, Hasan and Husayn, covered them with a cloak, then said: {Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly}. He said: And it was revealed concerning them. None introduced Amr ibn Qays between Sufyan and Zubayd in this hadith except Ubayd ibn Sa'id al-Umawi; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated it from Sufyan from Zubayd."
"3805","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you enter the mosque with arrows, hold their blades so you do not wound any of the Muslims. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Waki', and no one from Waki' except Sahl ibn Zanjalah."
"3806","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: My uncle Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: On the day of Badr the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed three while they were bound: he killed al-Nadr ibn al-Harith of Banu Abd al-Dar, he killed Tu'aymah ibn Adi of Banu Nawfal, and he killed Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bishr except Sufyan ibn Husayn; Husayn ibn Numayr was alone in transmitting it."
"3807","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rawwad narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created creation He sent Jibril, who divided people into two divisions: He divided the Arabs as a division and the non-Arabs as a division, and Allah's choice was among the Arabs; then He divided the Arabs into two divisions: Yemen as a division and Mudar as a division, and Quraysh as a division, and Allah's choice was among Quraysh; then He brought me forth from the best of those among whom I am. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Bishr ibn Mu'adh was alone in transmitting it."
"3808","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the last days there will be a people who blacken their hair; Allah will not look at them on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Abd al-Karim, and no one from Abd al-Karim except Hisham; Abd al-Wahhab was alone in transmitting it."
"3809","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Khallad al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the group who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were the jinn of Nasibin; they came to him at Nakhlah. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Zuhayr, and no one from Zuhayr except Khallad al-Ju'fi; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting it."
"3810","Ali ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss, then go out to prayer without renewing ablution. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Yazid ibn Sinan; Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi was alone in transmitting it from his father."
"3811","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from al-Hakam, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam who said: Uthman forbade mut'ah and joining Hajj with Umrah; that reached Ali, so he came out saying: Here I am for Hajj and Umrah together. Uthman said to him: Did I not forbid this? He said: I would not abandon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anyone's prohibition. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab except Ali ibn Hashim, and no one narrated it from Ali ibn Hashim except Abbad ibn Ya'qub."
"3812","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a dwelling branding camels, and he said: Has the daughter of Milhan given birth? I said: Yes, and I handed the boy to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Abu Dawud, and no one narrated it from Abu Dawud except Abd Allah ibn Imran."
"3813","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul - and I think from al-Zuhri - from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks the disgrace of Quraysh, Allah will disgrace him. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and no one from Muhammad except Abbad; Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Mada'ini was alone in transmitting it."
"3814","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Kulthum ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sidrah narrated to us, that Ata al-Khurasani narrated to him, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recitation at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except Kulthum ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sidrah."
"3815","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Nakha'i narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Ata, from A'ishah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until his feet swelled, and it was said to him: Do you do this though you have been forgiven? He said: Shall I not be a grateful servant? No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman except Yahya ibn Zakariyya al-Nakha'i; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"3816","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Rafi' Abu Hujr narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Amiri narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made permission-seeking in prayer glorification for men and clapping for women. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq except Ali ibn Abd Allah al-Amiri."
"3817","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah ibn Ma'bad al-Juhani narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ma'bad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated to me, from his uncle Harmalah ibn Abd al-Aziz who said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Sabrah ibn Ma'bad: that he attended Uhud with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was struck by a thrown stone in his leg and remained lame from it until he died. This hadith is not narrated from Sabrah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Fulayh was alone in transmitting it."
"3818","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Walid ibn Hazim al-Ummi al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Adi ibn Hatim who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who earned anger are the Jews, and the astray are the Christians. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Abd Allah ibn Ja'far was alone in transmitting it."
"3819","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform Hajj and Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Hamzah al-Zayyat, and no one from Hamzah except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting it."
"3820","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Dawud al-Burullusi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Hamzah al-Zayyat narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah al-Zayyat except Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah."
"3821","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan from Mis'ar except Abu Musa al-Ansari, and no one narrated it from Mis'ar except Sufyan and Abu Yahya al-Himmani; Yahya al-Himmani was alone in transmitting it from his father."
"3822","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Mughirah al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ata ibn Maysarah, that Abu Nadrah narrated to him, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr with them, then stood among them as a preacher and said in his sermon: Verily this world is green and sweet, and Allah is making you stewards in it, observing how you act; beware of this world and beware of women. Every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to his treachery, at his backside; and the greatest treachery is that of a ruler over the people. Anger is an ember kindled upon the heart of the son of Adam; do you not see him when he is angry how his eyes redden and his jugular veins swell? Whoever feels any of that, if standing let him sit, and if sitting let him cling to the ground. People in anger are of ranks: a man quick to anger, quick to calm - that is neither for him nor against him; a man slow to anger, slow to calm - that is neither for him nor against him; a man slow to anger, quick to calm - that is for him; and a man quick to anger, slow to calm - that is against him. The son of Adam is created in stages: a servant is created a believer, lives a believer, and dies a believer; a servant is created a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever; one is created a believer, lives a believer, and dies a disbeliever; and one is created a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a believer. And he mentioned that people in seeking dues are of ranks: a man when he seeks is harsh, and when sought from he pays - that for that; a man when he seeks withholds, and when sought from is taken from - that for that; a man when he seeks withholds yet takes, and when sought from he pays - that is better for him; and a man when he seeks withholds, and when sought from he delays - that is worse for him. Perhaps one of you sees wrong and does not change it; before you sixty-nine nations have passed, and you complete seventy; what has passed of this world compared to what remains is like what has passed of this day of yours compared to what remains. That was when the sun had yellowed and was setting. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except al-Husayn ibn Waqid; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"3823","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abd al-Salam al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn Mahbub narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When Abu Talib died, they seized their opportunity against the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O uncle, how quickly I have felt your loss. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, and no one from Abu Bakr except Furat ibn Mahbub; Isa ibn Abd al-Salam was alone in transmitting it."
"3824","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay' narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Makhul and Busr ibn Ubayd Allah, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: My maternal uncle, my mother's brother, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of our rites on this day is prayer, then sacrifice after prayer. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered my sacrifice before praying, wishing to have a meal ready for my neighbors, and I have a young goat dearer to me than the meat of two sheep - shall I slaughter it? He said: Yes, but it will not suffice anyone after you. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Zayd ibn Waqid; Muhammad ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"3825","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Najih narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided the people of Khaybar while they were going out in the morning; they were watching and said: Muhammad and the army, Muhammad and the army. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When we alight in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah."
"3826","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Musa ibn Maysarah, from Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas, from his father who said: al-Abbas sent Abd Allah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a need; he found a man with him, so he returned without speaking to him. He said: Did you see him? He said: Yes. He said: That was Jibril; he shall not die until his sight goes and he is granted knowledge. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Maysarah except Thawr ibn Yazid; al-Darawardi was alone in transmitting it."
"3827","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Wathilah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There are six traits; no Muslim dies in any one of them except that Allah guarantees to admit him to Paradise: a man who goes out striving, and if he dies on his way Allah guarantees him; a man who follows a funeral, and if he dies on his way Allah guarantees him; a man who visits a sick person, and if he dies on his way Allah guarantees him; a man who performs ablution well then goes out to a mosque for his prayer, and if he dies on his way Allah guarantees him; a man who comes to a ruler only to honor and revere him, and if he dies on that way Allah guarantees him; and a man in his house who backbites no Muslim, brings upon himself neither anger nor blame - if he dies on that way Allah guarantees him. No one narrated this hadith from Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla except Amr ibn Qays; al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman was alone in transmitting it."
"3828","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abd Allah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyah shall enter the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except al-Hakam ibn Bashir."
"3829","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray much standing and sitting; when he prayed standing he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting he bowed sitting. None introduced Muhammad ibn Sirin between Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah and Budayl al-Uqayli in this hadith except Muhammad ibn Sawa; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf was alone in transmitting it."
"3830","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Janab al-Qassab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: Suraqah ibn Malik stood up to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about our deeds that we do: are we seized for them at the outset - good for good and evil for evil - or is it something decreed beforehand and the pens have dried upon it? He said: O Suraqah, it has been decreed beforehand and the pens have dried upon it. He said: Then for what do we work, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Work, O Suraqah, for every worker is eased toward that for which he was created. He said: O Suraqah, now strive hard. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah except Abu Janab; Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath was alone in transmitting it."
"3831","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ali al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Hamalah, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Ibn al-Simt who said: I heard Bilal say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when I am intimate with my wife and we undress but I do not ejaculate, shall I bathe? He said: Yes; I did that with my wife and did not ejaculate, and we bathed. No one narrated this hadith from Bilal except Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, nor from Shurahbil except Ibn Muhayriz, nor from Ibn Muhayriz except Ali ibn Abi Hamalah; Damrah was alone in transmitting it."
"3832","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Attab Abu Bakr al-A'yan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: It was only revealed upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Your wives are a tilth for you} as a concession for approaching from behind. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Yahya ibn Sa'id; Muhammad ibn Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"3833","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-A'yan narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar who said: Uthman wanted him for judgeship but he refused, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Judges are three: one saved and two in the Fire: whoever judges unjustly or by desire is ruined, and whoever judges with truth is saved. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"3834","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ali al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When {The host will be defeated and turn their backs} was revealed, I said: Which host is this? Then on the day of Badr I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the sword unsheathed in his hand, saying: {The host will be defeated and turn their backs}. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Ma'mar, and no one from Ma'mar except Abd al-Majid; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ansari was alone in transmitting it."
"3835","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadham, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is prompted with La ilaha illa Allah at death shall enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Abu al-Ahwas."
"3836","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Talid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahhaf, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the valley floor while the people took the pass; then seven veiled men came. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them - Hudhayfah was leading and Ammar was ahead - he said: Bar what is beside you two. They did nothing. The Messenger of Allah looked at them and said: O Hudhayfah, do you know who the people are? I said: I know none of them except the owner of the red camel, for I know he is so-and-so. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Abu al-Jahhaf, and no one from Abu al-Jahhaf except Talid; Abbad was alone in transmitting it."
"3837","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Sa'id, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sacrifice two rams. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zubayr ibn Adi except Anbasah, and no one from Anbasah except Harun ibn al-Mughirah; Muhammad ibn Humayd and Zunayj al-Razi were alone in transmitting it."
"3838","Ali ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qahtani shall surely drive people with his staff. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Salamah ibn al-Fadl was alone in transmitting it."
"3839","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Abidi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prescribed penalty is upon the slave woman until she is fortified by marriage; when she is fortified, upon her is half of what is upon free chaste women. None raised this hadith from Sufyan except Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Abidi."
"3840","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: Artah Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one is greater in favor to me than Abu Bakr al-Siddiq; he supported me with himself and his wealth, and married his daughter to me. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Artah Abu Hatim; Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran was alone in transmitting it."
"3841","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Husayn al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Uthman who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution three times each. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ma'mar, and no one from Ma'mar except Yahya ibn Yaman; Abu Husayn al-Razi was alone in transmitting it."
"3842","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Amr al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Na'il ibn al-Qa'qa' ibn al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad al-Bahili narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, who said: My father came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with me along, and my father said to him: Supplicate to Allah for me and my son. He said: So he wiped my head and pledged him upon Islam. This hadith is not narrated from al-Hirmas except with this chain; Shabab al-Usfuri was alone in transmitting it."
"3843","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Durays narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon a freshly buried grave and said: Whose grave is this? It was said: The grave of so-and-so. So he prayed over him, and I was among those who prayed over him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Ibrahim ibn Tahman, and no one narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Tahman except Yahya ibn al-Durays and Muhammad ibn Humayd."
"3844","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people abandon jihad except that Allah envelops them in punishment. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Malik ibn Mighwal, and no one from Malik except Qabisah; Uqbah ibn Qabisah was alone in transmitting it."
"3845","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man owns a share in a slave and frees him, he guarantees the shares of his partners. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except Mus'ab ibn Sallam; Abbad ibn Ya'qub was alone in transmitting it."
"3846","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One Umrah to the next is expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. None introduced Suhayl ibn Abi Salih between Ubayd Allah ibn Umar and Sumayy in this hadith except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"3847","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: My father and Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None hears the call in this mosque of mine then leaves it except for a need, then does not return to it, except a hypocrite. No one narrated this hadith connected from Abu Hurayrah from Safwan and Abu Hazim except Ibn Abi Hazim; Abu Mus'ab was alone in transmitting it."
"3848","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until Allah is disbelieved in openly, and that is when they speak about their Lord. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Isma'il."
"3849","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Nu'man al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn al-Kumayt narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Sayf narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord that I marry into no one, and no one marry into me, except that he be with me in Paradise, and He granted me that. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ammar ibn Sayf, and no one from Ammar except Yazid ibn al-Kumayt; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Nu'man was alone in transmitting it."
"3850","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar al-Barra narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Awsajah narrated to me, he said: Matar Abu Musa, freedman of the family of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah gathered, and I was sitting with them as a boy. He said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, people claim I lie about the Messenger of Allah; what earth would carry me and what sky would shade me? He said: You are better than that. Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If people take a valley and the Ansar take a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar. Ibn Umar said: I have heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say it. Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not for emigration I would be a man of the Ansar. He said: You spoke truth; I heard him say it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He narrated nothing that day except that he confirmed him. He said: And I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall come to Hell and strike its gate, and it will be opened for me; I shall enter and praise Allah with praises no one before me praised Him with the like, nor shall anyone after me praise Him; then I shall bring out of it whoever said La ilaha illa Allah sincerely. Then some people of Quraysh will rise toward me and be attributed to me; I shall recognize their lineage but not know their faces, and I shall leave them in the Fire. He said: And I heard Abu Hurayrah say: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three, which I have not abandoned since I parted from him, nor shall I abandon them until I meet him: fasting three days of every month, the forenoon supererogatory prayer, and not sleeping except upon witr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Abbas ibn Awsajah except Abu Ma'shar al-Barra; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari was alone in transmitting it."
"3851","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ward ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to me, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ikrimah, from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting; and which of you had more control of his desire than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Ward ibn Abd Allah was alone in transmitting it."
"3852","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ward ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Yunus ibn Ubayd and Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Salih, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri was standing praying toward a pillar of the mosque when a man of the family of Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt passed before him; he prevented him, then he returned, so he pushed his chest. The youth complained, then came to Marwan ibn al-Hakam and complained to him about Abu Sa'id. Abu Sa'id came to him, and Marwan said to him: What is wrong with your brother's son complaining about you? Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you prays, let him pray toward a screen; if someone passes before him let him prevent him, and if he returns let him fight him, for he is a devil. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Adi ibn al-Fadl and Abd al-Warith; Ward ibn Abd Allah was alone in transmitting it from Adi ibn al-Fadl. And Abd al-Samad his son was alone in transmitting it from Abd al-Warith. None narrated it from Abd al-Samad except his son Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad. None narrated it from Ayyub except Adi ibn al-Fadl and Kharijah ibn Mus'ab; Ward ibn Abd Allah was alone in transmitting it from Adi ibn al-Fadl. And Abdan ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it from Kharijah ibn Mus'ab."
"3853","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing house snakes. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except al-Hakam ibn Fudayl; Abu al-Nadr was alone in transmitting it."
"3854","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Kindi al-Himsi narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Musawir the poet narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wondrous is the affair of the believer: all his affair is good for him, and that is only for the believer - if good befalls him and he is grateful it is good for him, and if evil befalls him and he is patient it is good for him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Musawir except Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Himsi."
"3855","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalaf ibn Ishaq ibn Mirsal al-Khath'ami narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isma'il ibn Mirsal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man, I think from Qays, came and said: O Messenger of Allah, curse Himyar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him; he came from the other side and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him; then he came from the other side and turned away; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on Himyar: their hearts are submission, their deeds are peace, their hands are food; people of security and faith. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Isma'il ibn Mirsal; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"3856","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abu Awwam, from Abd Allah ibn Musahiq who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You shall raise armies. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: Upon you is al-Sham, for it is Allah's choicest of His lands; in it are His choicest servants; whoever dislikes that, let him join his Yemen and water from his ponds, for Allah has guaranteed me al-Sham and its people. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"3857","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sallam al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting for stealth or plunder. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan except Umar ibn Muhammad; Sa'id ibn Sallam was alone in transmitting it."
"3858","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Dhawwad al-Harithi narrated to us, from Dhawwad ibn Ulbah, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When twelve of Banu Amr ibn Ka'b perish, there shall be mutual killing and slaughter until the Hour comes. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Tufayl except Ibn Khuthaym, nor from Ibn Khuthaym except Dhawwad ibn Ulbah, nor from Dhawwad except Isma'il ibn Dhawwad."
"3859","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn ... narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ishaq except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd."
"3860","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Ya'juj and Ma'juj? He said: Ya'juj is a nation and Ma'juj is a nation, each nation four hundred thousand nations; no man dies until he sees a thousand males before him from his loins, each one bearing arms. I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us? He said: They are three kinds: a kind among them like the arz. I said: What is the arz? He said: A tree in al-Sham, the tree a hundred and twenty cubits tall into the sky. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are those whom neither trick nor iron can withstand; and a kind among them spread one ear as a bed and cover themselves with the other; they pass by no elephant, wild beast, camel or pig except they eat it, and whoever of them dies they eat him; their vanguard is in al-Sham and their rear in Khurasan; they drink the rivers of the east and the lake of Tiberias. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and no one from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar."
"3861","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, from Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Maysarah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained he would take a handful of black seed. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar was alone in transmitting it."
"3862","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from Kurayb the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Umm Salamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast Saturday and Sunday more than any days, saying: They are two feast days of the polytheists, and I love to differ from them. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Baqiyyah was alone in transmitting it."
"3863","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Rawh - and he is Fulayt - from Jasrah bint Dajajah, from A'ishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say at the end of every prayer: O Allah, Lord of Jibril, Mika'il and Israfil, protect me from the heat of the Fire and from the punishment of the grave. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except al-Sabbah ibn Muharib; al-Husayn ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"3864","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muslim ibn al-Haytham al-Mu'addib narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Bakr ibn Wa'il narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed that I said: I shall surely stand the night and fast the day as long as I live. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you the one who said: By Allah I shall surely fast the day and stand the night as long as I live? I said: I have said it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You cannot bear that; pray and sleep, fast and break fast, and fast three days of every month, for a good deed is ten like it - that is like fasting eternity. I said: I can bear better than that. He said: Then fast a day and break fast two days. I said: I can bear better than that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast a day and break fast a day, and that is the fast of Dawud, and it is the most just of fasting. I said: I can bear better than that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing better than that. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Wa'il except Ya'la ibn al-Harith, and no one from Ya'la except his son; Ali ibn Muslim al-Mu'addib was alone in transmitting it."
"3865","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Habib ibn Thabit ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The last words the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke were: Succeed me well in my Household. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah except al-Zubayr ibn Habib; Ya'qub ibn Humayd was alone in transmitting it."
"3866","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tujibi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting he would not pray until we brought him fresh dates and water, and he would eat and drink when there were fresh dates; in winter he would not pray until we brought him dry dates and water. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd al-Tawil except Yahya ibn Ayyub, and no one from Yahya except Miskin ibn Abd al-Rahman; Zakariyya ibn Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"3867","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Rashid ... narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Rummanah narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: When Suhayl ibn Amr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: You shall not desist until I send to you a man who strikes your necks upon religion. Some said: Am I he, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No. Another said: Am I he? He said: No, but he is the mender of the sandal - and Ali was mending the sandal. Ali said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Qays ibn Rummanah said: Then I met Rib'i ibn Hirash, and he narrated it to me from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as Abu Burdah had narrated it to me. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except Qays ibn Rummanah, and no one narrated it from Qays ibn Rummanah except Yazid ibn Rashid, and no one from Yazid ibn Rashid except Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra; al-Husayn ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"3868","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Attab al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Abu Awanah, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allotted to Uthman from the spoils of Badr though he did not attend Badr. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Mawhab except Abu Awanah; Abu Qutaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"3869","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mu'min ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard something, so he preached and said to the Ansar: Were you not lowly and Allah honored you through me? Were you not astray and Allah guided you through me? Were you not fearful and Allah secured you through me? Will you not answer me? They said: With what shall we answer you? He said: You say: Did your people not expel you and we sheltered you; did your people not disbelieve you and we believed you? And he enumerated against them. He said: So they knelt upon their knees and said: Our wealth and selves are yours. Then was revealed: {Say: I ask you no reward except affection for kin}. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb; Abd al-Mu'min ibn Ali was alone in transmitting it."
"3870","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Anas al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None preserves the forenoon prayer except one oft-returning to Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Amr ibn Humran."
"3871","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hassan al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, made this city sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and fashioned it when He fashioned the sun and the moon; whatever faces it of the heaven is sacred. It was not lawful for anyone before me, and it was made lawful for me for an hour of the day, then it returned as it was. It was said to him: This is Khalid ibn al-Walid killing. He said to him: Rise, O so-and-so, go to Khalid ibn al-Walid and tell him to lift his hand from killing. The man went to him and said to him: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Kill whomever you can. So he killed seventy people. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he sent to Khalid ibn al-Walid: Did I not forbid you from killing? He said: So-and-so came to me and commanded me to kill whomever I could. So he sent to him: Did I not command you to command Khalid not to kill anyone? He said: You intended a matter and Allah intended a matter, and Allah's command was above your command, and I could do only what happened. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent toward him and answered him nothing. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Shu'ayb ibn Safwan."
"3872","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) burned some of the properties of Banu al-Nadir. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan was alone in transmitting it."
"3873","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa ibn Rashid al-Mustamli and Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili narrated to us, from Masad ibn Uqbah, from Yahya ibn Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talhah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity upon the poor is charity, and upon the kin is charity and joining ties. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Ishaq except Masad ibn Uqbah, and no one narrated it from Masad except Umar ibn Ayyub; Harun ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn Ammar were alone in transmitting it. And it is not narrated from Abu Talhah except with this chain."
"3874","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Harun al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abd Allah who said: Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would command us, while we were with him, not to remove our leather socks for three days and their nights except from major impurity, but from stool, urine and sleep. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ayyub ibn Suwayd; Ubayd Allah ibn Harun al-Firyabi was alone in transmitting it."
"3875","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from his father, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Nakhl, and he prayed Zuhr with us; the polytheists intended them, then said: Leave them, for they have after this a prayer dearer to them than their children. So Jibril came down and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr with his companions. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Harith ibn Umayr and Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id; none narrated it from al-Harith ibn Umayr except his son Hamzah ibn al-Harith; Bakr ibn Khalaf was alone in transmitting it."
"3876","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Isma'il al-Tayalisi al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Mubashshir narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches Ramadan and does not fast it is wretched; whoever reaches his parents or one of them and does not honor them is wretched; and whoever is mentioned before him and does not send blessings upon me is wretched. No one narrated this hadith from al-Fadl ibn Mubashshir except Abu Zuhayr."
"3877","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Suddi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The honor of a letter is its seal. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Yahya ibn Talhah was alone in transmitting it."
"3878","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather who said: We were with Abd Allah ibn Umar, and they mentioned the pilgrims of the people of Yemen and what they do therein; one of the people reviled them, so Ibn Umar said: Do not revile the people of Yemen, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The adornment of pilgrims are the people of Yemen. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Mu'adh ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali was alone in transmitting it."
"3879","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Nuh ibn Amr ibn Huwayy al-Saksaki al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Umamah who said: Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Tabuk and said: O Muhammad, attend the funeral of Mu'awiyah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Muzani. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and Jibril descended with seventy thousand angels; he placed his right wing upon the mountains and they lowered, and placed his left wing upon the lands and they lowered, until he looked toward Makkah and Madinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Jibril and the angels prayed over him. When he finished he said: O Jibril, by what did Mu'awiyah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Muzani attain this rank? He said: By reciting {Say: He is Allah, One} standing, sitting, walking and riding. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ziyad except Baqiyyah; Nuh ibn Amr al-Himsi was alone in transmitting it."
"3880","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Tanukhi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather al-Furat, from Abu al-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, from Zayd ibn Harithah who said: I was a boy in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come with us to a man whose affair we have seen. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out walking with his companions until they entered two walls in a long lane, reaching a small door at the far end of the lane; they entered a house and saw none in the house but a woman sitting, and a great waterskin full of water. They said: We see a waterskin but see no bearer. They spoke to the woman, and she pointed to a blanket in a corner of the house, saying: Look under the blanket. They uncovered it, and beneath it was a man. He raised his head, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May the face be disfigured. He said: O Muhammad, why do you insult me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I have concealed something for you; tell me what it is? And he said to his companions: I have concealed for him Surat al-Dukhan. He said: Surat al-Dukhan? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Be gone; what Allah wills shall be. Then he left. No one narrated this hadith from Furat al-Qazzaz except his son al-Hasan, and no one from his son except his son Ziyad; Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Tanukhi was alone in transmitting it."
"3881","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Mazdad ibn Jamil al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran al-Zahri narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Sulayman al-A'mash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Masruq ibn al-Ajda' who said: A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither sheep, nor camel, nor dinar, nor dirham, nor bequeathed anything. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn al-Harith except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"3882","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Atiq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi', from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: The people sighted the crescent, so I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I had seen it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted and commanded the people to fast it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi' except Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Salim, and no one from Yahya except Ibn Wahb; Marwan al-Tatari was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"3883","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Salamah al-Awsi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Salih ibn Hayy narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: Night prayer is two by two, and the salutation ... No one narrated this hadith from Mughirah except Ali ibn Salih, and no one from Ali except Salamah al-Awsi; Yahya ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"3884","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa, from his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that Jibril brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) al-Buraq, carried him before him, and set out with him. When he reached a low place its forelegs lengthened and its hind legs shortened until it leveled with him; when he reached a high place its forelegs shortened and its hind legs lengthened until it leveled. Then a man appeared on the right of the road calling to him: O Muhammad, to the road - twice. Jibril said: Proceed and speak to no one. Then a man alone appeared on the left of the road saying to him: To the road, O Muhammad - twice. Jibril said to him: Proceed and speak to no one. Then a beautiful, comely woman appeared. Jibril said to him: Do you know who the man on the right of the road was? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. He said: Those were the Jews; they called you to their religion. Then he said: Do you know who the man who called you on the left of the road was? He said: No. He said: Those were the Christians; they called you to their religion. Do you know who the beautiful, comely woman was? He said: That was this world; it called you to itself. Then we set out until we came to Bayt al-Maqdis, and there was a group sitting; when they saw him they said: Welcome to Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet. Among the sitting group was an elder. Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this? He said: This is your father Ibrahim. Then he asked him and said: Who is this? He said: Musa. Then he asked him: Who is this? He said: This is Isa son of Maryam. Then prayer was established, and they pushed one another until they put Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forward. Then drinks were brought, and Muhammad chose milk. Jibril said to him: You have hit the natural disposition. Then it was said to him: Rise with me to your Lord. So he rose and entered, then came back. He said to him: What did you do? He said: Fifty prayers were prescribed upon my nation. Musa said to him: Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation, for you cannot bear this. So he returned, then came back. Musa said to him: What did you do? He said: He reduced them to twenty-five prayers. Musa said to him: Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation, for your nation cannot bear this. So he returned, then came back until He reduced them to five. Musa said to him: Return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said: I am too shy before my Lord to return to Him, and He has said to me: For every return you returned, you have a request I shall grant you. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abi Layla except with this chain; Harun ibn al-Mughirah was alone in transmitting it."
"3885","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Sa'd ibn Abi al-Dayr al-Nasri narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Mujahid, from A'ishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to rulers, woe to trustees, woe to overseers; there shall come upon one of them a day when he wishes he were hung from a star forever and had never ruled over two. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Umar ibn Sa'd; Isma'il ibn Musa was alone in transmitting it."
"3886","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj al-Bahili, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A'ishah wanted to buy Barirah and free her, but her owners said: No, unless you make wala for us. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Buy her, for wala belongs only to whoever frees. So she bought her and freed her. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: What is wrong with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition not in the Book of Allah, it is void. He said: She was under a slave of Banu al-Mughirah called Mughith, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the choice. He said: And Ibn Abbas narrated that Abu Bakr narrated: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) imposed upon her the waiting period of a free woman. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj al-Bahili and Hammam ibn Yahya, and no one from al-Hajjaj except Mu'tamir; Muhammad ibn Jami' was alone in transmitting it. And Hammam did not mention in his hadith the report of Ibn Abbas from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq."
"3887","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Mut'im ibn al-Miqdam al-San'ani narrated to me, from Abu Sawrah the nephew of Abu Ayyub, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a copper idol and struck its back with the back of his hand, then said: Ruined and lost is whoever worships you besides Allah. Then Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with an angel; the angel stepped aside. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with him that he stepped aside? He said: He smelled copper from you, and we cannot bear the smell of copper. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mut'im ibn al-Miqdam except Yazid ibn Yusuf; Marwan ibn Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"3888","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the campaign of Hunayn with eighteen nights past of Ramadan, while fasting; they passed by a river and stared hard at it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Will you drink? They said: Shall we drink while you are fasting? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel and drank. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the campaign of Hunayn and al-Ta'if, he came to al-Ji'ranah, divided the spoils there, and performed Umrah from it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Bashir; Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd was alone in transmitting it."
"3889","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when reciting while sitting, if a verse remained he would stand, recite it, then bow. No one narrated this hadith from Matar al-Warraq except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"3890","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abu Bishr Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr said to Mu'awiyah in the dispute that occurred between them over the pledge to Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah: And you, O Mu'awiyah, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When there are two caliphs on earth, kill one of them. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr except Sa'id ibn Jubayr, nor from Sa'id except Abu Bishr, nor from Abu Bishr except Sa'id ibn Bashir; Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd was alone in transmitting it."
"3891","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalaf ibn Ishaq ibn Mirsal al-Khath'ami narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: My uncle Isma'il ibn Mirsal narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marked the grave of Uthman ibn Maz'un with a rock. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Isma'il ibn Mirsal; Amr ibn Khalaf was alone in transmitting it."
"3892","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: My uncle Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from A'ishah who said: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him this supplication in witr: O Allah, guide me among those You guided, bless for me what You gave, and protect me from the evil of what You decreed; for You decree and none decrees upon You, and whoever You befriend is never disgraced; blessed are You our Lord and exalted. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Musa ibn Uqbah, and no one narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah except his nephew Isma'il ibn Ibrahim; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from A'ishah from al-Hasan ibn Ali except with this chain."
"3893","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Ma'bad ibn Shaddad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Mujahid who said: I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: How little your food is? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Ali ibn Ma'bad, and it is not narrated from Mujahid from Abu Sa'id except with this chain."
"3894","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: al-Khasib ibn Nasih narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Dawud, from al-A'mash, from Dharr, from Yusay' al-Hadrami, from al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: {Those who are too proud for My worship} - he said: for My supplication - {shall enter Hell humbled}. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Khasib ibn Nasih."
"3895","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the house snakes. And he said: Each of you is a shepherd responsible for his flock: the ruler over people is a shepherd responsible for his flock; a man is a shepherd over his family responsible for them; a man's wife is a shepherdess over her husband's house responsible for it; a man's slave is a shepherd over his master's wealth responsible for it. Verily each of you is a shepherd and each is responsible for his flock. None narrated in this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar from Abu Lubabah except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Dinar; Abu Mus'ab was alone in transmitting it."
"3896","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Khazzaz al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Subayh al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Ibrahim al-Hariri narrated to us, from Abd al-Mu'min ibn al-Qasim al-Ansari, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Imran ibn Maytham, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Are you not pleased, O Ali, when the prophets are gathered on one plain, bare, barefoot, walking, their necks cut by thirst, and the first called is Ibrahim, clothed in two white garments, then standing at the right of the Throne; then a stream from Paradise bursts toward my Pool - my Pool wider than between Busra and Sanaa, in it as many as the stars of the sky, cups of silver - so I drink and perform ablution, then I am clothed in two white garments, then I stand at the right of the Throne; then you are called, so you drink, perform ablution, are clothed in two white garments, and stand with me; and I am not called to any good except you are called to it."
"3897","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Khazzaz al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Ibrahim al-Hariri narrated to us, from Abd al-Mu'min ibn al-Qasim al-Ansari, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Sa'id Abu al-Bakhtari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a young boy and do not judge well. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand between my shoulders and said: Allah shall guide your heart and make your tongue firm. Ali said: I never struggled with judging between two until I sat in this seat of mine. None narrated these two hadiths from Aban ibn Taghlib except Abd al-Mu'min ibn al-Qasim; Sufyan ibn Ibrahim al-Hariri was alone in transmitting them."
"3898","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two, and when you fear dawn, make witr with one. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except al-Hakam ibn Fudayl; Abu al-Nadr was alone in transmitting it."
"3899","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Shu'ayb al-Nahwi al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: Rashdin ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; what exceeds is charity."
"3900","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Attab al-Tayalisi al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: Rashdin ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man grants his son a gift and the son takes possession of it, then the father becomes needy, the son has more right to it; and if the son had not taken possession of it and the father becomes needy, the father has more right to it."
"3901","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Isma'il al-Tayalisi al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: Rashdin ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman shall not give charity from her husband's house except with his permission. None narrated these reports from Rashdin ibn Kurayb from his father except Abu Zuhayr."
"3902","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Bakkar al-Barrad al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Adi ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu al-Haytham, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Bishr ibn Numayr, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends upon himself an expenditure to preserve his chastity, it is charity; and whoever spends upon his wife, child and household, it is charity."
"3903","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Adi ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The likeness of one who returns in his gift is like the dog: it ate until sated, then vomited, then returned to it and ate it. None narrated these two hadiths from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Adi ibn Abd al-Rahman, nor from Adi except al-Zubaydi, nor from al-Zubaydi except Muhammad ibn Harb, nor from Muhammad except al-Rabi' ibn Rawh; Imran ibn Bakkar was alone in transmitting them."
"3904","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Asim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Dhakwan the freedman of A'ishah, from A'ishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the two units after Asr, yet forbid them. No one narrated this hadith from Dhakwan except Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, and no one from Muhammad ibn Amr except Ibn Ishaq; Abu Zuhayr was alone in transmitting it."
"3905","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Raja ibn Abi Salamah, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy who said: Our commander Ishaq ibn Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab recited this verse {Today I have perfected your religion for you} with Ka'b beside him; Ka'b said: I know a people of religion upon whom, had it been revealed in a day, they would have taken it as a festival. Umar said: It was revealed on the evening of Arafah, a Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Raja ibn Abi Salamah except Damrah."
"3906","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Asim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father Zayd ibn Harithah: that Jibril descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the first of what was revealed to him, and taught him ablution; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he took his hand and sprinkled his private part with water. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth except Sa'id ibn Shurahbil; the well-known version is from the hadith of Ibn Lahi'ah."
"3907","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qatan al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, treat Mu'awiyah well, for he is trustworthy over the Book of Allah, and an excellent trustworthy one he is. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Marwan; Muhammad ibn Qatan was alone in transmitting it."
"3908","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite Ya-Sin in the dawn prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Shu'bah and Ayyub ibn Jabir, and no one narrated it from them except Abu Dawud; Abd Allah ibn Imran was alone in transmitting it."
"3909","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in Zuhr and Asr: {By the heaven and the night-comer} and {By the heaven with towers}. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hammad ibn Salamah, and no one from Hammad except Abu Dawud; Abd Allah ibn Imran was alone in transmitting it."
"3910","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Khawwas narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah said: Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Zarir al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the last days there shall be a trial; people shall be sifted as gold is sifted in the mine. Do not revile the people of al-Sham, but revile their wicked; for among them are the Abdal. Soon a cause from heaven shall be sent upon the people of al-Sham, splitting their unity, until if foxes fought them they would overcome them. Then an outsider from my Household shall emerge with three banners; the frequent say: they are fifteen thousand, and the few say: they are twelve thousand. Their signs are: kill, kill. They shall meet seven banners, under each banner a man seeking kingship; Allah shall kill them all, and Allah shall restore to the Muslims their unity, blessing, far and near. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Lahi'ah except Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa."
"3911","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Musarrif ibn Amr al-Yami narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Buraydah ibn Sufyan narrated to me, from Ibn al-Baylamani, from Kurz ibn Alqamah who said: A delegation of the Christians of Najran, sixty riders, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); among them twenty-four of their nobles, and among the twenty-four were three men to whom their affair returned: al-Aqib, the trustee of the people, their counselor, whose opinion and command they followed, named Abd al-Masih; al-Sayyid, their scholar, their caravan leader and gathering head; and Abu Harithah ibn Alqamah, brother of Bakr ibn Wa'il, their bishop, rabbi, imam and archer chief. Abu Harithah had been honored among them for his diligence in their religion, and the Roman Christian kings had honored, accepted, built churches for, and bestowed favors upon him. When they set out from Najran toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Harithah mounted a mule heading to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with his brother Kurz ibn Alqamah beside him riding along; Abu Harithah's mule stumbled, so Kurz said: Perish the far one - meaning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Rather you perish. He said: Why, O brother? He said: By Allah, he is indeed the Prophet we awaited. Kurz said to him: What prevents you, knowing this? He said: What these people have done for us: they honored, appointed and favored us, and they refuse but to oppose him; were I to do it they would strip from us all you see. His brother Kurz ibn Alqamah concealed it from him - meaning he embraced Islam thereafter. This hadith is not narrated from Kurz ibn Alqamah al-Bakri - not al-Khuza'i - except with this chain; Yunus ibn Bukayr was alone in transmitting it."
"3912","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Qariz from al-Agharr except Sa'id ibn Khalid, nor from Sa'id ibn Khalid except Ibn Abi Dhi'b, nor from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Dinar; Mus'ab was alone in transmitting it."
"3913","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qaddah narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Anas narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad except Abu Bahr; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari was alone in transmitting it."
"3914","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: Artah Abu Hatim narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Karimah who said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib addressing upon the pulpit of Kufah, saying: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Beware of the dress of monks, for whoever lives as a monk and imitates is not of me. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran was alone in transmitting it."
"3915","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: We were such that none was more deserving of being preferred by his brother than his brother. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3916","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Kufi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's spending on his family is charity. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"3917","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurra, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam; in it is food for nourishment and healing for sickness. And by Allah, there is no water on the face of the earth worse than the water of a well in the valley of Barahut, like locust legs among vermin; in the morning it gushes forth and in the evening there is no moisture in it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Hurra except Muhammad ibn Muhajir, nor from Muhammad ibn Muhajir except Miskin ibn Bukayr; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb was alone in transmitting it."
"3918","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mabad ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh, from Abdullah ibn Alqama ibn Abi al-Faghwa, from Ibn Umar, from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd, from Hafsa, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not declare anything unlawful through breastfeeding except ten sucklings, or odd ten. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sad; al-Waqidi was alone in transmitting it."
"3919","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tarsusi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Said al-Musahiqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra, from Uthman ibn Affan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends to cause a servant to deviate, He blinds him to stratagems. This hadith is not narrated except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"3920","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Nafi, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak about the private converse? Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah will draw the servant near to Him on the Day of Resurrection, and place His shelter and His veil over him from the people, and make him confess his sins, saying: Do you acknowledge such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. And He will say: Do you acknowledge such-and-such sin? He will say: Yes, my Lord. Then when He has made him confess his sins and he sees that he is ruined, He will say: I have concealed them for you today. He said: Then he will be given the record of his good deeds. He said: As for the hypocrite and the disbeliever, he will be called out over the heads of the witnesses: These are those who lied against their Lord. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Malik ibn Mighwal, and no one narrated it from Malik ibn Mighwal except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughira."
"3921","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Umar al-Jinni narrated to us, he said: al-Mualla ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about palm trees, and he said: They are those firmly rooted in mud, and those that feed in drought."
"3922","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ismail ibn Raja narrated to us, from his father, he said: I was in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a circle in which were Abu Said al-Khudri and Abdullah ibn Amr, when al-Husayn ibn Ali passed and greeted, and the people returned the greeting, but Abdullah ibn Amr remained silent. Then Ibn Amr raised his voice after the people had fallen silent and said: And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Then he turned to the people and said: Shall I not inform you of the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of heaven? They said: Yes. He said: It is this one walking away. By Allah, I have not spoken a word to him, nor has he spoken a word to me, since the nights of Siffin. And by Allah, for him to be pleased with me is more beloved to me than for me to have the like of Uhud. Abu Said al-Khudri said to him: Will you not go to him in the morning? He said: Yes. So they agreed to go to him in the morning, and I went with them. Abu Said sought permission and it was granted, so we entered, and he sought permission for Ibn Amr and kept at it until al-Husayn gave him permission, so he entered. When Abu Said saw him he moved aside for him, while he was sitting beside al-Husayn, and al-Husayn drew him to himself. Ibn Amr stood and did not sit, and when he saw that, he left Abu Said and made room for him, and he sat between them. Abu Said recounted the story and said: Is it so, O Ibn Amr? Do you know that I am the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of heaven? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Kaba, you are indeed the most beloved of the people of the earth to the people of heaven. He said: What carried you to fight me and my father on the day of Siffin? By Allah, my father is better than me. He said: Yes, but Amr complained about me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Abdullah stands the night in prayer and fasts the day. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray and sleep, fast and break fast, and obey Amr. Then when the day of Siffin came, he adjured me, and by Allah I did not swell their numbers, nor did I draw a sword for them, nor thrust with a spear, nor shoot an arrow. Al-Husayn said to him: Did you not know that there is no obedience to a created being in disobedience to the Creator? He said: Yes. He said: So it was as if he accepted it from him. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Raja except Hashim ibn al-Barid, and no one narrated it from Hashim except his son Ali ibn Hashim; Abbad ibn Yaqub was alone in transmitting it."
"3923","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama and Hammad ibn Zayd and Yazid ibn Ibrahim and Shuba and Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, all of them from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Does not the one who raises his head while the imam is prostrating fear that Allah will turn his head into the head of a donkey? No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Abd al-Malik al-Juddi; Muhammad ibn Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"3924","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Uqba narrated to us, from Hamza al-Zayyat, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wear white garments, for they are purer and better, and shroud your dead in them. No one narrated this hadith from Hamza except al-Walid; Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"3925","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Shabi, he said: Abu Juhayfa said: I entered upon Ali in his house and said: O best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Gently, woe to you, O Abu Juhayfa. Shall I not inform you of the best of people after the Messenger of Allah? Abu Bakr, and Umar. Woe to you, O Abu Juhayfa, love for me and hatred of Abu Bakr and Umar do not gather in the heart of a believer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid except al-Fadl ibn al-Mukhtar, nor from al-Fadl except Idris ibn Yahya; Nasr ibn Marzuq was alone in transmitting it."
"3926","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Atiq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Safwan al-Qasim ibn Yazid ibn Awana narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Siyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan except Hassan ibn Siyah, nor from Hassan except al-Qasim ibn Yazid Abu Safwan; Abd al-Salam ibn Atiq was alone in transmitting it."
"3927","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Ghusn narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hosting one of the two litigants to the exclusion of the other. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except al-Qasim ibn Ghusn; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz was alone in transmitting it."
"3928","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Ghusn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is Friday, send abundant blessings upon me, for your blessings are presented to me, and ask al-Wasila for me. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Wasila? He said: The highest rank with me in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except al-Qasim ibn Ghusn; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz was alone in transmitting it."
"3929","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman, Luwayn, narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar al-Barra narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abdullah ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: I heard Muawiya in Mecca on the day of Ashura saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted it, so whoever among you has not fasted it, let him fast it. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Uthman except Abu Mashar al-Barra; Luwayn was alone in transmitting it."
"3930","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Tahrani narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ubaydullah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Salim, from Mujahid, from Aisha, that something belonging to her was stolen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard her supplicating, so he said: Do not invoke evil against him. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Ismail ibn Salim, nor from Ismail except Abu Awana, nor from Abu Awana except Hisham ibn Ubaydullah; Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Tahrani was alone in transmitting it."
"3931","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Zaytuni, from the people of al-Zaytuna, narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian; if they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Isa ibn Yunus, nor from Isa except Amr ibn Uthman; Muhammad ibn al-Abbas was alone in transmitting it."
"3932","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Zaytuni narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in Tabuk for twenty nights, shortening the prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Isa, nor from Isa except Amr ibn Uthman; Muhammad ibn al-Abbas was alone in transmitting it."
"3933","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabia, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Injury by a dumb animal is without liability, and the well is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Layth ibn Sad except Yaqub ibn Ibrahim."
"3934","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Harun ibn Abdullah, from Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard a man saying: Ha, Khadira! So he said: O, here I am at your service; we have taken your good omen from your mouth; go out with us to Khadira. So they went out to it, and no sword was drawn in it. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir ibn Abdullah except Harun ibn Abdullah; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in transmitting it."
"3935","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muawiya ibn Maysara ibn Shurayh narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Utayba narrated to us, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the doors to be closed except the door of Ali. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you closed all the doors except the door of Ali? He said: I did not close your doors, but Allah closed them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Muawiya ibn Maysara; Suwayd ibn Said was alone in transmitting it."
"3936","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talha al-Qannad narrated to us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: My ears heard and my heart retained the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever claims belonging to other than his father while knowing his father, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him. No one narrated this hadith from Musa al-Juhani except Mindal ibn Ali; Amr ibn Hammad was alone in transmitting it."
"3937","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Mismar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out and proclaim among the people: From Allah, not from His Messenger: Allah has cursed the cutter of the lote tree. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, except Ibrahim ibn Yazid, nor from Ibrahim except Hisham ibn Sulayman."
"3938","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu Qatada, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever takes hair, let him treat it well or let him shave it. And Abu Qatada used to groom his hair every other day. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"3939","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim Abu Yafur narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, that Ali came on the day of Basra with gold or silver, and he poked it and said: Become white and become yellow, and deceive other than me; deceive the people of Syria tomorrow when they prevail over you. His saying that weighed heavily upon the people, and that was mentioned to him, so he called out among the people and they entered upon him. He said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ali, you will come to Allah and your partisans pleased and pleasing, and your enemy will come to Him angry and with heads raised. Then Ali gathered his hand to his neck, showing them how raising the head is. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Tufayl except Jabir; Abd al-Karim Abu Yafur was alone in transmitting it."
"3940","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mabad ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you stands for prayer, let him devote himself to it until he finishes from it, and beware of turning in prayer, for one of you converses privately with his Lord as long as he is in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ruman except Nafi ibn Thabit; al-Waqidi was alone in transmitting it."
"3941","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Isa Abu Isa al-Harrani narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever approaches a mahram woman in intercourse will not enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb except Abd al-Karim, nor from Abd al-Karim except Abd al-Aziz ibn Isa; Muhammad ibn Mihran was alone in transmitting it."
"3942","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted conversed privately with Musa in one hundred and forty thousand utterances over three days, all of them counsels. When Musa heard the speech of human beings he found it distasteful because of what had fallen upon his hearing of the speech of the Lord. And among what He confided to him was that He said: O Musa, those who seek to impress have never sought to impress Me with anything like renunciation of the world, and those who seek nearness to Me have never sought nearness with anything like abstinence from what I have forbidden them, and worshippers have never worshipped Me with anything like weeping from fear of Me. Musa said: O God of all creation, O Master of the Day of Judgment, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, what have You prepared for them, and what have You rewarded them? He said: O Musa, as for those who renounce the world, I permit them My Paradise, to dwell wherever they wish. As for those who abstain from what I have forbidden them, there is no servant who meets Me on the Day of Resurrection but that I press him in reckoning and press him about what was in his hands, except the abstinent, for I am shy before them and honor them, and I admit them to Paradise without reckoning. As for those who weep from fear of Me, theirs is the highest companionship, in which none share. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Abu Malik al-Janbi was alone in transmitting it."
"3943","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Talha narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Jabir ibn Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: This religion will remain sound; whoever opposes it or contends against it will not harm it, until twelve rulers rule, all of them from Quraysh. No one narrated this hadith from Mabad ibn Khalid except Ishaq ibn Talha; Bishr ibn al-Walid was alone in transmitting it."
"3944","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Umar al-Jinni narrated to us, he said: Zaida ibn Abi al-Ruqad narrated to us, he said: Ziyad al-Numayri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When Rajab entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, bless us in Rajab and Shaban, and bring us to Ramadan. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Zaida ibn Abi al-Ruqad was alone in transmitting it."
"3945","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: Umm Sulaym bint Milhan, the mother of Anas ibn Malik, narrated to me, from her mouth to my ear, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Umm Salama, and I found men with him, so I sat until they stood. When he came out I drew near to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, a matter that draws me near to Allah about which I love to ask you, since I am in doubt about it. He said: You have done right, O Umm Sulaym. I said: Should a woman bathe if she sees in her dream what a man sees? Umm Salama said: May your hands be dusty, O Umm Sulaym, you have exposed women. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather may your hands be dusty, O Umm Salama. Do you think, were it not for that, the child would resemble its father? Yes, if you see that, then bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Umama ibn Sahl except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, nor from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra was alone in transmitting it."
"3946","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Hisinjani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was granted victory by the easterly wind, and Ad were destroyed by the westerly wind. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from al-Minhal, except Sharik; Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik was alone in transmitting it."
"3947","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Mamar ibn Abdullah ibn Nadla, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None hoards except a wrongdoer. None inserted al-Zuhri between Yahya ibn Said and Said ibn al-Musayyab in this hadith except Hammad ibn Salama, nor from Hammad except Muammal ibn Ismail; Muammal ibn Ihab was alone in transmitting it."
"3948","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Israil narrated to us, from al-Numan, from al-Awzai, from Salim, from Sudaysa the freedwoman of Hafsa, from Hafsa, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and I had vowed to celebrate with a tambourine if he returned from Mecca: While I was thus, Umar sought permission, so I took the tambourine to the side of the house and covered it with a cloak. I said: O Prophet of Allah, you are more deserving to be held in awe. He said: Satan does not meet Umar since he embraced Islam except that he falls upon his face. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except al-Numan, and he is Abu Hanifa, and no one narrated it from Abu Hanifa except Israil; al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq was alone in transmitting it. And Ishaq ibn Sayyar al-Nasibi narrated it from al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq, from Israil, from al-Awzai, and he did not mention al-Numan."
"3949","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Wahb ibn Khunays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: An Umra in Ramadan equals a Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Ghaylan ibn Jami except Yala ibn al-Harith; Yahya ibn Yala was alone in transmitting it."
"3950","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ayan, from Mamar, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you awaits but enriching wealth that transgresses, or poverty that causes forgetfulness, or corrupting illness, or debilitating old age, or sudden death, or the Dajjal, and the Dajjal is the worst awaited absentee, or the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Ibrahim ibn Ayan, nor from Ibrahim except Israil, nor from Israil except Ibrahim ibn al-Mukhtar; Muhammad ibn Humayd was alone in transmitting it."
"3951","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Qazaa ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, he said: Suwayd ibn Hujayr narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed under a blind banner, calling to partisanship and aiding his partisans, his killing is that of ignorance. No one narrated this hadith from Suwayd ibn Hujayr except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj; Qazaa ibn Suwayd was alone in transmitting it."
"3952","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered into his prayer and we said takbir with him, and he gestured to the people: Stay as you are. We remained standing until the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, having bathed, his head dripping water. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Said, nor from Said except Muadh; Ubaydullah ibn Muadh was alone in transmitting it."
"3953","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayya narrated to us, he said: Mujahid narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The wedding feast is a right and a sunna, so whoever is invited and does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. The khurs, the idhar, and the tawkir are up to you. He said: I said: By Allah, I do not know what al-khurs, al-idhar, and al-tawkir are? He said: Al-khurs is for childbirth, al-idhar is for circumcision, and al-tawkir is when a man builds a house and settles among people and prepares food and invites them; they have the choice, if they wish they answer, and if they wish they stay back. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Umayya except Yahya ibn Uthman al-Taymi; al-Salt ibn Masud was alone in transmitting it."
"3954","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zanja al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab al-Ukli narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn Uqba al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Maymun al-Hadrami narrated to me, he said: Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted Abu Bakr and Umar, and they advised him, and Abu Bakr was right. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umar, Allah dislikes that Abu Bakr should err. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Sad except with this chain; Zayd ibn al-Hubab was alone in transmitting it."
"3955","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mundhir Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik: That he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying upon a donkey while going to Khaybar, praying with the qibla behind him. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Qays, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, except Ismail ibn Umar. And Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated it from Dawud, from Yahya ibn Said, and he did not mention Muhammad ibn Ajlan."
"3956","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Abu Nubata Yunus ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Three things my beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me: two prostrations before dawn, the two of Duha, and witr after Isha. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla except Salama ibn Wardan; Abu Nubata was alone in transmitting it."
"3957","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, Ibn Idris said: And I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whatever intoxicates a faraq of it, an uqiyya of it is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Layth, nor from Layth except Ibn Idris; Ali ibn Said was alone in transmitting it. And people narrated it from Layth, from Abu Uthman, whose name is Amr ibn Salim, from al-Qasim, from Aisha."
"3958","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Abu al-Ala al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One of you says to his wife: I have divorced you, I have taken you back. This is not the divorce of the Muslims; divorce the woman at the approach of her purity. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb."
"3959","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid, and people narrated it from Ibn Jurayj from Musa ibn Uqba."
"3960","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas, from Thumama, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve of Duha, a house will be built for him in Paradise. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ishaq was alone in transmitting it."
"3961","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Zarbi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn al-Khuzai, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you swears an oath and then sees another better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath. This hadith is not narrated from Imran ibn al-Husayn except with this chain; Said ibn Zarbi was alone in transmitting it."
"3962","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Aisha: That she was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with her dolls. Abu Usama did not narrate any supported hadith from Abd al-Razzaq other than this."
"3963","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Qatada, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of innovation are the worst of creation. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except al-Muafa; Muhammad ibn Ammar was alone in transmitting it."
"3964","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That he used to pray four before Friday and four after it. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab ibn Bashir."
"3965","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mutarrif ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Excellence of knowledge is better than excellence of worship, and the best of your religion is scrupulousness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus."
"3966","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us with his face red, while we were disputing about a verse of the Quran. He said: What is this you are engaged in? We said: A verse of the Quran about which we disputed. He said: Do not dispute about the Quran, for disputing about the Quran is disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Fulayh ibn Sulayman."
"3967","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Salama Yahya ibn Khalaf al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Yala ibn Hakim, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lizard? He said: I do not eat it nor do I forbid it. No one narrated this hadith from Yala ibn Hakim except Said ibn Abi Aruba."
"3968","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Dhari narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the time of Isha? He said: When the night fills the belly of every valley. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Jafar ibn Sulayman."
"3969","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubayda ibn Man al-Masudi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from al-Harith ibn Abi Ziyad, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyenas have devoured us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Something other than that is more fearful to me for you: when the world is poured upon you in abundance. Would that my umma not wear gold. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Ubayda ibn Man; his son was alone in transmitting it from him."
"3970","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Rafi Abu Hujr narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Said ibn Wahb, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Aisha said: O Messenger of Allah, And those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful: Are they those who err and commit sins? He said: No, O Aisha, they are those who pray and give charity while their hearts are fearful. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except al-Hakam ibn Bashir."
"3971","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dahir al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman was created from a rib; her likeness is that of a rib: if you straighten it you break it, and if you leave it, it remains crooked. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus."
"3972","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysara al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who strikes cheeks, tears garments, and calls with the call of ignorance. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus."
"3973","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqa, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to come to a tree between Mecca and Medina, and alight beneath it, claiming that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqa except Marwan ibn Muawiya."
"3974","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Isam ibn Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man came to Ibn Umar and asked him about jarred date-wine? He said: That is of what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden. Then he came to Ibn Abbas and informed him of what Ibn Umar said, and he said: Ibn Umar spoke the truth."
"3975","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysara, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah indeed raises the servant by good character to the rank of fasting and prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Budayl ibn Maysara except Hammad ibn Salama; Habban ibn Hilal was alone in transmitting it."
"3976","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Sinan al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels submitted willingly, the Ansar submitted willingly, and Abd al-Qays submitted willingly. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Uqba ibn Sinan was alone in transmitting it."
"3977","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari and Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days of every month, witr before sleep, and the two rakahs of Duha. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Tayyah except Abd al-Warith."
"3978","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham al-Bakka narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Abu Talib fell ill and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited him. He said to him: O son of my brother, supplicate your God whom you worship to heal me. He said: O Allah, heal my uncle. Abu Talib stood as if released from bonds, and said to him: O son of my brother, your God whom you worship indeed obeys you. He said: And you, my uncle, if you obey Allah, He will indeed obey you. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except al-Haytham ibn Jammaz, nor from al-Haytham except Sharik ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi; Uqba ibn Mukram was alone in transmitting it."
"3979","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: al-Mughira bint Hassan al-Tamimiyya informed me, she said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd and bathe with a sa. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughira bint Hassan except Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"3980","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sanani narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Uyayna narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Yala, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: Abu Talha ordered two mudds of barley to be prepared, then sent me to invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came to him and invited him. He said to those with him: Stand. I walked before him until I entered upon Abu Talha. He said: What have you done? I said: I invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to the people: Stand. Abu Talha said: You have exposed us before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); did you not know what we have? I said: Yes, but I could not say anything to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached the door, he entered ten by ten, spoke as Allah willed, then said: Eat. When they were full they went out, and ten entered, until eighty men ate from it, and there remained of it what sufficed the household. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Imran ibn Uyayna."
"3981","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Tarif Abu Sufyan al-Utaridi narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah the Exalted says: Bring out of the Fire whoever had in his heart the weight of a grain of barley of faith. Then He says: Bring out of the Fire whoever had in his heart the weight of a grain of mustard of faith. Then He says: By My might, I will not make one who believed in Me for an hour of night or day like one who did not believe in Me. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Harith except Abu Sufyan al-Sadi; Marwan ibn Muawiya was alone in transmitting it."
"3982","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazza narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Umara ibn Zadahn narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Umara ibn Zadahn; Muammal ibn Ismail was alone in transmitting it."
"3983","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazza narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Umara ibn Zadahn narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Muslims were routed on the day of Hunayn, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon his gray mule, whose name was Duldul, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Duldul, brace yourself. She pressed her belly to the ground until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a handful of dust and threw it in their faces, and said: Ha-Mim, they will not be aided. The people were routed, though we did not shoot them with an arrow, nor thrust with a spear, nor strike with a sword. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Umara ibn Zadahn; Muammal was alone in transmitting it."
"3984","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Rabia ibn Uthman, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you come to Friday, bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Rabia ibn Uthman except Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"3985","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to Friday, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Uthman except his son."
"3986","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mutarrif, from Atiyya, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A neck will emerge from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, with an eloquent tongue, calling: I have been entrusted today with three: with every obstinate tyrant, whoever sets up another god with Allah, and whoever kills a soul without a soul. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Amr ibn Abi Qays and Salih ibn Umar al-Wasiti."
"3987","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abi al-Zubayr al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Abu Yazid al-Thumali narrated to me, from Tawus ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, a thousand times, has ransomed himself from Allah, and the end of his day will be as one freed by Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Tawus ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad was alone in transmitting it."
"3988","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by children and greeted them. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan; Bishr ibn Hilal was alone in transmitting it."
"3989","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Muslim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I shall inform you of the affairs of people and their characters: A man is quick to anger and quick to return, so nothing is against him nor for him; it is even. A man is slow to anger and quick to be pleased, so that is for him and not against him. A man is quick to anger and slow to be pleased, so that is against him and not for him. A man takes what is his and gives what is upon him, so that is neither against him nor for him; it is even. A man gives what is upon him and does not take what is his, so that is for him and not against him. A man takes what is his and withholds from people what is theirs, so that is against him and not for him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Sharik; his son Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it."
"3990","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and each of them brought upright witnesses in equal number. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast lots between them and said: O Allah, judge between them. No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr ibn Abdullah except Usama ibn Zayd, nor from Usama except Ibn Abi Hazim; Abu Musab was alone in transmitting it."
"3991","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrating, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: We alighted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); among us were those saying takbir and among us those saying tahlil, and neither did those saying takbir find fault with those saying tahlil, nor those saying tahlil with those saying takbir. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Mutamir ibn Sulayman."
"3992","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn al-Barid narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, and al-Hasan and al-Husayn, or one of them, came and mounted upon his back. When he prostrated he raised his head; he said with his hand, and he held him, or held them both. Then he said: What an excellent mount is your mount. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Fudayl ibn Marzuq, nor from Fudayl except Ali ibn Hashim; Abbad ibn Yaqub was alone in transmitting it."
"3993","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Musab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at al-Aswaf, with Bilal with him, and he let his feet dangle into the well and uncovered his thighs. Abu Bakr came seeking permission, and he said: O Bilal, give him permission and give him glad tidings of Paradise. Abu Bakr entered and sat to the right of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dangling his feet into the well and uncovering his thighs. Then Umar came seeking permission, and he said: Give him permission, O Bilal, and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He entered and sat to the left of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dangling his feet into the well and uncovering his thighs. Then Uthman came seeking permission, and he said: Give him permission, O Bilal, and give him glad tidings of Paradise despite a trial that will befall him. Uthman entered and sat facing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dangling his feet into the well and uncovering his thighs. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, except al-Darawardi; Abu Musab was alone in transmitting it."
"3994","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Farra al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam and Nafi, from Ibn Umar: That he used to say the talbiya: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; there is no partner for You. And he narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sad; al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam was alone in transmitting it."
"3995","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Fever is from the blast of Hell, so cool it with water. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Said, nor from Said except Rawh; Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi was alone in transmitting it."
"3996","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Nubata al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Zaida and Attab ibn Ayan and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib, and he was not untruthful, saying: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he raised his head from bowing, none of us bent his back until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his forehead upon the ground. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Zaida and Attab ibn Ayan except Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri; Muhammad ibn Nubata was alone in transmitting it."
"3997","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Busra bint Safwan, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever touches his private part and his testicles, let him perform ablution as for prayer. None said in this hadith, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Busra: and his testicles, let him perform ablution as for prayer, except Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar; Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani was alone in transmitting it."
"3998","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Dawud al-Qantari narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Sulayman al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Alqama al-Bayruti narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans; whoever meets them and buys, its owner has more right to it when he arrives. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Uqba ibn Alqama, nor from Uqba except al-Harith ibn Sulayman; Ali ibn Dawud was alone in transmitting it."
"3999","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim ibn al-Bara, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: Abu Sufyan passed by with Muawiya behind him, and he was a man seeking aid. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, deal with the wielder of spears. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn al-Bara except Salama ibn Kuhayl, nor from Salama except Ibn Ishaq; Salama ibn al-Fadl was alone in transmitting it."
"4000","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from al-Mughira ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from al-Ward ibn Muawiya, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about monkeys and pigs, and he said: Allah never grew angry at a people and then gave them offspring or progeny. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid al-Dalani except Abd al-Salam ibn Harb."
"4001","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, from Khallad al-Saffar, from al-Ashath ibn Taliq, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Murra al-Hamdani, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may my father be ransomed for him, announced his own death to us a month before his death. When parting drew near, he gathered us to him in the house of our mother Aisha. Then he looked at us, his eyes filled with tears, and he composed himself and said: Welcome to you; may Allah greet you, may Allah have mercy on you, may Allah shelter you, may Allah aid you, may Allah raise you, may Allah benefit you, may Allah guide you, may Allah provide for you, may Allah grant you success, may Allah keep you safe, may Allah accept you. I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, and I entrust you to Allah, and I leave Him as guardian over you. I am to you from Him a clear warner. Do not exalt yourselves over Allah among His servants and in His lands, for Allah said to me and to you: That is the Home of the Hereafter; We assign it to those who desire no exaltation in the land nor corruption, and the outcome is for the God-fearing. And He said: Is there not in Hell a lodging for the arrogant. Then he said: The term has drawn near, and the return to Allah, and to Sidrat al-Muntaha, and to the Garden of Refuge, and to the Highest Companion, and the fullest cup, and fortune and pleasant life. We said: Who will wash you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Men of my household, the nearest then the nearest. We said: How shall we shroud you? He said: In these garments of mine, if you wish, or in a Yemeni cloak, or in Egyptian white. We said: Who will pray over you among us? We wept and he wept, then he said: Gently; may Allah forgive you and reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. When you have washed me and shrouded me, place me upon my bier in this house of mine at the edge of my grave, then leave me for a while, for the first to pray over me will be my companion and close friend Jibril, then Mikail, then Israfil, then the Angel of Death with his hosts. Then enter upon me in companies, and pray over me and salute with salutation, and do not harm me with a wailing woman, nor clamor, nor lament. Let the men of my household and their women begin the prayer over me, then you. Convey my greeting much to my companions who are absent, for I have greeted whoever pledged to me upon my religion until the Day of Resurrection. We said: Who will place you in your grave? He said: My family, with many angels; they will see you whence you do not see them. No one perfected the chain of this hadith except Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi. And al-Muharibi narrated it from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Asbahani, from Murra, from Abdullah. He did not mention Khallad al-Saffar, nor al-Ashath ibn Taliq, nor al-Hasan al-Urani."
"4002","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Fayyad al-Zimmani narrated to us, he said: Halbas ibn Muhammad al-Dubai narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata and Nafi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The sick person prays standing; if hardship befalls him he prays sitting; if hardship befalls him he prays lying down gesturing with his head; if hardship befalls him he glorifies. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Halbas; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Fayyad was alone in transmitting it."
"4003","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Zanjala narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz, from Ayman, the freedman of Ibn Abi Amra, he said: I entered upon Aisha while I was then a slave, before I was freed, and I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, at which hour did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray most? She said: From the sun's decline until it inclines. No one narrated this hadith from Ayman, and he is Abu Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman, except Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz; al-Sabbah ibn Muharib was alone in transmitting it."
"4004","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Utba Abu Muadh al-Basri narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Fatima came and stood beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), facing him. He said: Come near, O Fatima. She drew near a step. Then he said: Come near, O Fatima. She drew near a step. Then he said: Come near, O Fatima. She drew near until she stood before him. Imran said: I saw pallor appear upon her face and the blood had gone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spread his fingers, then placed his palm between her collarbones, raised his head, and said: O Allah, Feeder of the hungry, Fulfiller of need, Raiser of the lowly, do not let Fatima bint Muhammad hunger. I saw the pallor of hunger leave her face and the blood appear. Then I asked her after that, and she said: I have not hungered after that, O Imran. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrima except Utba Abu Muadh; Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Imran ibn Husayn except with this chain."
"4005","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Firdaws ibn al-Ashari narrated to us, he said: Masud ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aisha, that she went out for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and menstruated, and she did not become pure until she reached Mina and Arafat, and completed the rites of Hajj. Then she circumambulated the Kaba afterwards, and between al-Safa and al-Marwa. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her brother: Take her out of the Sanctuary and make her enter ihram for Umra. So he made her enter ihram from al-Tanim. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except Masud, nor from Masud except Firdaws; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting it."
"4006","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Muawiya ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the woman who tattoos and the one tattooed, the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined, the muhill and the one for whom tahleel is done, and the eater of usury and its feeder. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Huzayl, except Muawiya ibn Hisham. And people narrated it from Sufyan, from Abu Qays, from Huzayl."
"4007","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Hasan al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Hanan ibn Sudayr al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Sudayf al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, and I never saw any Muhammadi equal to him, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and I heard him saying: O people, whoever hates us, the People of the House, Allah will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection as a Jew. I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: Even if he fasts and prays and claims he is a Muslim. O people, with that he safeguards his blood from being shed, and that he pay the jizya readily while they are humbled. My umma was displayed to me in clay, and the bearers of banners passed by me, and I sought forgiveness for Ali and his partisans. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Abu Jafar, nor from Abu Jafar except Sudayf, nor from Sudayf except Hanan ibn Sudayr."
"4008","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi ibn Sulayman al-Muradi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Rassasi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a bow slung over her, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed women who imitate men and men who imitate women. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Muslim, nor from Muhammad ibn Muslim except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad."
"4009","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hashim al-Balabakki narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Qays ibn Abi Gharaza, he said: We were men in Medina buying wasqs in the market of Medina; we called ourselves, and people called us, brokers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called us by better than what we called ourselves, saying: O company of merchants, idle talk and oaths attend sale, so mix it with something of charity. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Shayban and Abu Hamza al-Sukkari; al-Walid ibn Muslim was alone in transmitting it from Shayban."
"4010","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of you are the best of you in character, and good character is of faith. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Suwayd; Muhammad was alone in transmitting it."
"4011","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit al-Zuhri al-Madini narrated to us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Musa informed me, from Musab ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayya, from Umm Salama, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave concession to Sahla bint Suhayl regarding breastfeeding in particular, but Umm Salama did not act upon it. No one narrated this hadith from Musab ibn Abdullah except al-Zubayr, nor from al-Zubayr except Abd al-Aziz; Abdullah ibn Marwan was alone in transmitting it."
"4012","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Alqama ibn Qays ibn Thalaba narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Umar kneading in prayer, leaning upon his hands when he stood. I said: What is this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kneading in prayer, meaning leaning. No one narrated this hadith from al-Azraq except al-Haytham; Yunus ibn Bukayr was alone in transmitting it."
"4013","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Qabisa ibn Jabir al-Asadi, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: I want to divide the Sawad of Kufa among the Muslims who prevailed. Sad wrote to him: O Commander of the Believers, we have prevailed over the softest-hearted people Allah created, the most generous in spirit, the greatest in blessing, the most open-handed; their hands are but food and their tongues but peace. If you deem fit, O Commander of the Believers, do not disperse them nor divide them, nor let them turn us from the course through which He granted us conquest. For the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The might of the Arabs lies in the points of their spears and the hooves of their horses. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Salih; Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban was alone in transmitting it."
"4014","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Nassar ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Asram ibn Hawshab al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All lands will vanish on the Day of Resurrection except the mosques, for they will join one to another."
"4015","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Nassar ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today is the wagering and tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise, and ruined is whoever enters the Fire. I am first, Abu Bakr is the second, Umar is third, and people after us are according to precedence, first then first. No one narrated this hadith from Qurra except Asram."
"4016","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Ruman al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr al-Laythi, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sunna is two sunnas: a sunna in an obligation and a sunna in other than an obligation. The sunna that is in the obligation has its basis in the Book of Allah; taking it is guidance and leaving it is misguidance. The sunna whose basis is not in the Book of Allah, taking it is a virtue and leaving it is not a sin."
"4017","And with it: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever does not perform witr has no prayer. That reached Aisha, and she said: Who heard this from Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? By Allah, the time is not distant, and I have not forgotten. Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: Whoever comes with the five prayers on the Day of Resurrection, having guarded their ablution, their times, their bowing and their prostration, diminishing nothing of them, comes with a covenant from Allah that He will not punish him. And whoever comes having diminished something of them has no covenant from Allah; if He wills He has mercy on him, and if He wills He punishes him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Muhammad except Isa; Abdullah was alone in transmitting them."
"4018","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Shayba al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ibn Shubruma, he said: I heard Khalid ibn Abdullah al-Qasri upon the pulpit saying: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Yazid ibn Asad, do not bring to people except what you love to be brought to you. No one narrated this hadith from Hushaym, from Ibn Shubruma, except Abd al-Rahman. And people narrated it from Hushaym, from Sayyar, from Khalid ibn Abdullah."
"4019","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, he said: When the strap of the sandal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke, he would walk in one, with the other in his hand, until he found a strap and wore them. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in transmitting it."
"4020","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya ibn al-Sakan al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Bishr ibn Umar; al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Asamm was alone in transmitting it."
"4021","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Harun al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I walked behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) testing whether he disliked that. He reached for me with his hand and brought me alongside. Then I lagged behind testing whether he disliked that. He reached for me with his hand and brought me alongside. Then I lagged behind testing him, and he reached for me with his hand and brought me alongside. So I knew that he disliked that. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid."
"4022","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Shayban al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in my mosque equals a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Abd al-Malik al-Juddi; Ahmad ibn Shayban was alone in transmitting it."
"4023","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Mughira al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abdullah ibn Masud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them that when a woman enters upon her husband, the man should stand and she should stand behind him, and they pray two rakahs, and he says: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless my family in me. O Allah, provide them from me and provide me from them. O Allah, unite us as long as You unite in good, and separate us when You separate toward good."
"4024","And with it, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Maqil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir over funerals seven, five, and four times, so say takbir as the imam says takbir when you have put him forward. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ata except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"4025","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Jammal al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to his companions: Let us go to Banu Waqif to visit al-Basir, and he was blind. None connected this hadith from Sufyan, from Amr, from Muhammad, from his father, except Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Jammal. And Husayn al-Jufi narrated it from Ibn Uyayna, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir."
"4026","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade green jars and hollowed stumps. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muthanna except Abu Dawud."
"4027","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with traces of mud upon his sandals, wearing a cloak, and he kept guarding lest it touch the cloak. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Abd al-Rahman; Abu Ali al-Hanafi was alone in transmitting it."
"4028","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Qazaa narrated to us, he said: Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about the children of polytheists? He said: Allah knows best what they would have done. No one narrated this hadith from Aththam except al-Husayn ibn Qazaa."
"4029","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Khalaf al-Asam narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Bilad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, he said: We were with Abu Said al-Khudri in the mosque, and a man turned over arrows. Abu Said said: Did this one not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade turning weapons about in the mosque and unsheathing them? No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Bilad except Marwan."
"4030","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Baqiyya narrated to us, he said: Utba ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim al-Ansari Abu Maryam narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the most tender-hearted. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni. Indeed tranquility and dignity are among the owners of sheep, and indeed arrogance and pride are among the owners of horses and camels, and the loud-voiced owners of wool. No one narrated this hadith from Utba ibn Abi Hakim except Baqiyya."
"4031","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Musa, from Maysara, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Musa except al-Dahhak; Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it."
"4032","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Bilal al-Sadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim al-Qasmali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take your shield, take your shield. They said: O Messenger of Allah, from an enemy present? He said: No, but from the Fire. Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as forerunners and flankers, and they are the enduring good deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Abd al-Aziz, and none narrated it from Abd al-Aziz except Abu Umar al-Hawdi and Ibn Bilal."
"4033","Ali narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Qadi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Mujahid, from Aisha, she said: A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he brought him near and drew his seat close. When he left him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not complain of this one? He said: Yes, but among the worst of people are those honored out of fear of their evil. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Sharik."
"4034","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumayla narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Iyas al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: I came to Ibn Umar, I and Umayya ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, and I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, when did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform witr? He said: At the end of the night. No one narrated this hadith from al-Salt ibn Iyas except Abd al-Mumin; Abu Tumayla was alone in transmitting it."
"4035","Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu al-Jarrah, the freedman of Umm Habiba, from Umm Habiba, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People will emerge from the east seeking a man at the House, until when they are at a desert land they will be swallowed. Those who lagged behind them will join them, and what befell them will befall them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one brought out under compulsion? He said: What befell the people will befall him, then Allah will resurrect each person upon his intention. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jarrah except Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, nor from Muhammad except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Salama ibn al-Fadl was alone in transmitting it."
"4036","And with it: Salama ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, answer him; and whoever gifts you a trotter, accept it. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Abu Jafar; Salama ibn al-Fadl was alone in transmitting it."
"4037","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Bahram at al-Rayy narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book, from Amr ibn Qays, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, wiped over the two socks, and prayed the prayers with one ablution. Umar said to him: You have done something you did not used to do? He said: I did it deliberately, O Umar."
"4038","And with it: From Amr ibn Qays, from al-Hakam, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. These two hadiths are not narrated from Amr except with this chain; Ismail ibn Bahram was alone in transmitting them."
"4039","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mabad ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Atiyya ibn Qays, from Ziyad ibn Jariya, from Habib ibn Maslama, he said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grant a fourth at the outset and a third upon return in a raid. No one narrated this hadith from Said, from Atiyya, except Zayd. And Abd al-Razzaq and others narrated it from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul."
"4040","And with it, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah protect you from rulers after me. He said: What of them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Whoever enters upon them, believes their lies and aids them in their tyranny is not of me, nor will he come to my Basin. Know, O Abd al-Rahman, that fasting is a shield and prayer is a proof. O Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, Allah the Exalted has refused me that flesh grown from unlawful earnings enter Paradise; the Fire is more deserving of it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Said ibn Bashir, nor from Said except Zayd ibn Yahya; Ali ibn Mabad was alone in transmitting it."
"4041","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn Raja narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite al-Waqia and the like of suras in dawn prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Israil, nor from Israil except Salama ibn Raja; Yaqub ibn Humayd was alone in transmitting it."
"4042","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Jayfar ibn al-Hakam al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Masud, from Malik ibn Damra, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the collection of charity, and men began coming with according to their wealth and their charity. I wept, and he said: O Abu Dharr, why do you weep? I said: The wealthy have carried off the reward. He said: How? I said: They pray as we pray, fast as we fast, and find what to give in charity, while we do not find. He said: Rather the wealthy are the lowest, except one who says with wealth thus and thus, and few are they. I said: How, O Messenger of Allah? He said: There is no owner of camels who does not pay their zakat in their milk and their aid except that they will come on the Day of Resurrection in a flat plain, trampling him with their hooves; whenever the first of them passes, the last returns upon him, until judgment is passed among people. I said: And horses, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Horses are for three groups: one who takes them as preparation in the path of Allah, for him is their hardship and their ease. By Allah, if they traverse a courtyard and climb one or two heights, they descend upon a green meadow. And one who takes them in arrogance, they will be a calamity upon him on the Day of Resurrection. They said: And donkeys, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Nothing was revealed about them except the singular verse: Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. No one narrated this hadith from Jayfar ibn al-Hakam except Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri; his son Tahir was alone in transmitting it."
"4043","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, he said: Sulayman, the freedman of Umm Salama, narrated to me, from Umm Salama, she said: A single vessel, about half a faraq, would be placed for me and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would begin before me, and we would bathe together. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn al-Hakam except Said ibn Zayd."
"4044","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Tamimi narrated to us, he said: Maqil ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the sun and it receded an hour of the day. No one narrated this hadith from Maqil except al-Walid; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it, and none narrated it from Abu al-Zubayr except Maqil."
"4045","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Nubata al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: Going out to the open ground for the two Eids is of the sunna."
"4046","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Sahl ibn Zanjala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: Reciting aloud in the prayer of the two Eids is of the sunna. No one narrated these two hadiths from Mutarrif except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"4047","Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah ibn Ulatha narrated to me, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Mujahid, from Jarir ibn Abdullah, he said: I only embraced Islam after al-Maida was revealed, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe after I embraced Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Abd al-Karim, nor from Abd al-Karim except Ziyad ibn Abdullah, nor from Ziyad except Abu al-Nadr; Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr was alone in transmitting it."
"4048","Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib: That Ali sold slaves and separated a woman from her son, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him and annulled the sale. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid except Abd al-Salam."
"4049","Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Katib narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to me, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Envy almost precedes decree, and need almost becomes disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman except Isa, nor from Isa except Amr ibn Uthman; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Katib was alone in transmitting it."
"4050","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antara, from his father, from Ali: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite upon the pulpit: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ibrahim ibn Khalid; Ishaq ibn Zurayq was alone in transmitting it."
"4051","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Atiyya ibn Baqiyya narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Magians of this umma are those who deny decree. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Awzai; Baqiyya was alone in transmitting it."
"4052","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Abu Layla, from Humayda bint al-Shamardal, from Qays ibn al-Harith: That he embraced Islam while having eight wives, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to choose four of them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful except Isa ibn Yunus; al-Sari ibn Asim was alone in transmitting it."
"4053","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talha al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women have no share in the middle of the road; let them seek its edges and not crowd it. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd ibn Umayr except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Muhammad ibn Talha; Abd al-Aziz was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ali except with this chain."
"4054","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, he said: Ubada ibn Nusayy informed us, from Kab ibn Ujra, from Salman, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Guarding a day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a month and standing it, and whoever dies guarding in the path of Allah is spared the trial of the grave, and his righteous work continues for him until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Kab ibn Ujra except Ubada ibn Nusayy, nor from Ubada except Hisham ibn al-Ghaz; al-Walid was alone in transmitting it."
"4055","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, the freedman of Banu Hashim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every child is born upon the fitra, until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian, just as camels are born complete; do you find among them any with cropped ears until you crop them? No one narrated this hadith from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar except Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd; Abd al-Warith was alone in transmitting it."
"4056","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shubruma narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khalil narrated to us, from Abu al-Saifa, from Jundub, he said: When the Kharijites parted from Ali, he went out seeking them, and we went out with him. We reached the camp of the people, and they had a hum like the hum of bees from reciting the Quran, and among them were owners of calluses and owners of hooded cloaks. When I saw them, doubt entered me from that, so I withdrew, planted my spear, dismounted my horse, laid my shield down, spread my armor upon it, took my horse's bridle, and stood praying toward my spear, saying in my prayer: O Allah, if fighting these people is obedience to You, then permit it, and if it is disobedience, then show me Your acquittal. While I was thus, Ali came upon the mule of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he drew level with me he said: Seek refuge with Allah from doubt, O Jundub. I hastened to him, and he dismounted and stood praying, when a man came upon a pony at a trot and said: O Commander of the Believers. He said: What do you want? He said: Do you need the people? He said: What of that? He said: They have crossed the river and gone. He said: They have not crossed it? I said: Glory be to Allah. Then another came swifter in running and said: O Commander of the Believers. He said: What do you want? He said: Do you need the people? He said: What of that? He said: They have crossed the river and gone. I said: Allah is Greatest. Ali said: They have not crossed it. Then another came urging his horse and said: O Commander of the Believers. He said: What do you want? He said: Do you need the people? He said: What of that? He said: They have crossed the river. Ali said: They have not crossed it, nor will they cross it, and they will surely be killed short of it; a covenant from Allah and His Messenger. I said: Allah is Greatest. Then I stood and held his stirrup for him, and he mounted his horse. Then I returned to my armor and wore it, and to my horse and mounted it. Then I placed my foot in the stirrup and went out riding beside him. He said to me: O Jundub. I said: At your service, O Commander of the Believers. He said: As for me, I shall send to them a man reciting the mushaf, calling them to the Book of their Lord and the sunna of their Prophet, and he will not turn his face to us until they shower him with arrows. O Jundub, indeed not ten of us will be killed, nor ten of them spared. We reached the people while they were in their camp where they were, not having moved. Ali called out among his companions and arrayed them, then came to the rank from one end to the other twice, saying: Who will take this mushaf and walk with it to them, calling them to the Book of their Lord and the sunna of their Prophet, while he will be killed, and Paradise is his? None answered him but a youth of Banu Amir ibn Sasa. When Ali saw his young age, he said to him: Return to your station. Then he called a second time, and none came out to him but that youth. Then he called a third time, and none came out to him but that youth. Ali said to him: Take it. So he took the mushaf. He said: You will indeed be killed, and you will not turn your face to us until they shower you with arrows. The youth went out walking with the mushaf to the people. When he drew near them where they could hear, they stood and began fighting before he returned. He said: A man shot him with an arrow, and he turned his face to us and sat down. Ali said: Take to the people. Jundub said: I killed with this hand of mine, after what had entered me of what had entered me, eight before I prayed Zuhr, and neither ten of us were killed nor ten of them spared, as he said. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Shubruma except Said ibn Khuthaym; Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari was alone in transmitting it."
"4057","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Fajr is in the protection of Allah, and his reckoning is upon Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Malik except Ismail; al-Haytham ibn al-Yaman was alone in transmitting it."
"4058","Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Shabib al-Musalli narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Isa narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication between the iqama and the adhan is not rejected. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Isa except Umar ibn Shabib; Abu Hisham was alone in transmitting it."
"4059","Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ayyub al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When three are on a journey, let one of them lead them. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym except Ziyad ibn Yunus."
"4060","Ali narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Abu Jabir narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Usayd Abu al-Yaqzan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mudrik al-Nakhai narrated to us, he said: Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My umma is a mercy-shown umma; there is no punishment upon it. Its punishment is only in the world: earthquakes, tribulations, and killing. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Mudrik except Umar ibn Usayd, nor from Umar except Abu Jabir; Ishaq ibn Zurayq was alone in transmitting it."
"4061","4056 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Bakr ibn Umarah ibn Ruwaybah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays before the rising of the sun and before its setting, and testifies that there is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise. An old man from the people of Basra heard it and said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, three times. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Amr; Ali ibn Hashim was alone in transmitting it, from his father."
"4062","4057 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Purify your courtyards, for the Jews do not purify their courtyards. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibrahim, nor from Ibrahim except Abu Dawud; Zayd ibn Akhzam was alone in transmitting it."
"4063","4058 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Abi Zayd al-Dabbagh narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of my umma is only like the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Dinar except Umar ibn Hafs; al-Husayn ibn Abi Zayd al-Dabbagh was alone in transmitting it."
"4064","4059 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abdillah al-Baqqal narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from al-Rabi ibn Umaylah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People on the Day of Resurrection are of four kinds, and deeds are of six kinds: among them is one for whom it is made spacious in this world and spacious for him in the Hereafter, and among them is one for whom it is made spacious in this world but restricted for him in the Hereafter, and among them is one for whom it is restricted in this world but made spacious for him in the Hereafter, and among them is one wretched in this world and the Hereafter; and deeds are: two that necessitate, and like for like, and tenfold, and seven hundredfold. As for the two that necessitate: whoever dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise, and whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire. As for like for like: whoever intends a good deed, and whoever does an evil deed. And tenfold: whoever does a good deed. And seven hundredfold: spending in the path of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Amr except al-Hakam ibn Bashir."
"4065","4060 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Attar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah; and Ayyub, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was lying across in front of him. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Dawud; Abd al-Ala was alone in transmitting it."
"4066","4061 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Uthman ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the black man hungers he steals, and when he is full he commits adultery; and they have two traits: truthful generosity, and courage. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yahya ibn Said was alone in transmitting it."
"4067","4062 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Zayrak Abu al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Awf ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one tells stories to the people except a commander, or one commanded, or one who affects it. No one narrated this hadith from Busr ibn Said and Sulayman ibn Yasar except Bukayr ibn Abdillah, nor from Bukayr except al-Dahhak; Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it."
"4068","4063 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ata, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about a man who has with him a voluntary sacrificial animal and it is injured before reaching its place. He said: He slaughters it, then smears its sandal with its blood, then strikes its side with it; but if he eats from it, its making up becomes obligatory upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wasiti was alone in transmitting it."
"4069","4064 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umarah and Khuthaym ibn Irak narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come out for the dawn prayer with his head dripping water, from intercourse without a wet dream, then he would begin the morning fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Yasar except Muhammad ibn Umarah and Khuthaym ibn Irak; Asim was alone in transmitting it from them both."
"4070","4065 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Ghafiqi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Khalid ibn Aslam, the freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to me, he said: I went out one day with Abdillah ibn Umar, and a bedouin caught up with him and said to him: The saying of Allah: {And those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend them in the path of Allah}. Ibn Umar said: Whoever hoards them and does not pay their zakat, then woe to him; this was only before zakat was revealed, but when it was revealed Allah made it a purification for wealth. Then he turned and said: I would not care if I had the like of Uhud in gold, knowing its amount, paying its zakat, and acting in it in obedience to Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uqayl, nor from Uqayl except Ibn Lahiah."
"4071","4066 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Marzuq al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Maslamah al-Qanabi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Dubai narrated to us, from Juwayriyah ibn Asma, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar heard a man saying: The miserly is more excusable than the wrongdoer. Ibn Umar said: You have lied; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The miserly will not enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Juwayriyah, nor from Juwayriyah except Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Dubai; Yahya ibn Maslamah al-Qanabi was alone in transmitting it, and he is the brother of Abdillah ibn Maslamah; they are three brothers: Abdillah, Yahya, and Ismail."
"4072","4067 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Isa al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Jahm ibn Aws narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Abi Maryam, while Abdillah ibn Rustum passed by him in his procession and said to Ibn Abi Maryam: I desire your company and your discourse; then when he had passed, Ibn Abi Maryam said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not envy a wicked man for a blessing, for you do not know what he will meet after his death; indeed he has with Allah a killer that does not die. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Abi Maryam except Jahm ibn Aws; Ibn al-Mubarak was alone in transmitting it."
"4073","4068 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abdillah al-Umawi narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata and Ibn Jurayj and Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: That a man wounded a man, and he wanted to take retaliation, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking retaliation from the wounder until the wounded one recovers. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn Ata and Uthman ibn al-Aswad except Abdillah ibn Abdillah al-Umawi; Yaqub ibn Humayd was alone in transmitting it."
"4074","4069 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Musa al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Abu Sad al-Baqqal, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: Take the throats of the people; may my father and mother be ransom for you. Sad would place his arrow in the middle of his bow and say: O Allah, Your arrow and in Your path; O Allah, help Your Messenger. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, answer Sad when he supplicates to You. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Sad except Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra."
"4075","4070 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Isa al-Juhani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has ninety-nine names; whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Hammad ibn Isa al-Juhani."
"4076","4071 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Dirar al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam ibn al-Bara ibn Qabisah al-Thaqafi informed me, he said: My father informed me, from Amir ibn Abd al-Asad al-Abqasi, from Abdillah ibn al-Ghasil, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he passed by al-Abbas and said: O uncle, follow me with your sons. So he went with six of his sons: al-Fadl, Abdillah, Ubaydullah, Abd al-Rahman, Qutham, and Mabad. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought them into a house and covered them with a black shawl of his striped with red, and said: O Allah, these are my household and my kindred, so screen them from the Fire as You have screened them with this shawl. He said: There remained in the house neither mud-brick nor door but that it said amen. This hadith is not narrated from Abdillah ibn al-Ghasil except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran was alone in transmitting it."
"4077","4072 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mutarrif al-Mughirah ibn al-Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is cursed, and cursed is what is in it, except a scholar or a learner, and the remembrance of Allah, and what supports it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban, from Abdah, except Abu al-Mutarrif; Bishr ibn Muadh was alone in transmitting it. And others narrated it from Ibn Thawban, from Ata ibn Qurrah, from Abdillah ibn Damrah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"4078","4073 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim Abu Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Usamah, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wretched is the slave of the dinar and the dirham, whose only concern is a dinar or a dirham that he obtains and takes. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Usamah except Abu Yahya al-Taymi."
"4079","4074 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The stars are a security for the people of heaven, and my Companions are a security for my umma. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except al-Sabbah; al-Husayn ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"4080","4075 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Sadusi narrated to us; Said ibn Abi Ka'b al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn the Quran and teach it to the people, and learn the laws of inheritance and teach them to the people; it is near that there will come upon the people a time when two men dispute over a law of inheritance and find no one to decide between them. No one narrated this hadith from Rashid except Said; Muhammad ibn Uqbah was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except with this chain."
"4081","4076 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Yasar, the freedman of Abdillah ibn Masud, narrated to me, he said: Husayn ibn Sadaqah ibn Yasar al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your children in righteousness; whoever wishes extracts disobedience for his child."
"4082","4077 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Husayn narrated to me, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aishah: O Aishah, abandon acts of disobedience, for it is the best emigration, and guard the prayers, for it is the best righteousness. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Maqburi except Husayn; Ibn Abi Bazzah was alone in transmitting them both, from Muhammad ibn Yahya."
"4083","4078 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Abd al-Hamid Abu Amr - and under him was Fatimah bint Qays and he divorced her - so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: There is no maintenance for her. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Hamid Abu Amr except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Khalid was alone in transmitting it."
"4084","4079 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Darda Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munib al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Rabiah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Rushayd narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, he said: Ikrimah narrated to me, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The chief of the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection is Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and a man who stood up to an unjust ruler, forbade him and commanded him, and he killed him. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Abu Hanifah, nor from Abu Hanifah except al-Hasan ibn Rushayd, nor from al-Hasan ibn Rushayd except Said; Abu al-Darda was alone in transmitting it."
"4085","4080 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Humayd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah ibn Sinan al-Himsi narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah indeed wards off affliction from a hundred households among his neighbors through a righteous Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except Hafs ibn Sulayman, nor from Hafs except Yahya; Abu Humayd al-Himsi was alone in transmitting it."
"4086","4081 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Masudi Abdillah ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Abdillah ibn Masud narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Hasirah narrated to us, from Sakhr ibn al-Hakam, from his uncle, that he heard Amr ibn al-Hamiq say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, and they said: O Messenger of Allah, you are sending us while we have no provisions, nor food, nor knowledge of the road. He said: You will pass by a man of bright face who will feed you food, give you drink, and guide you to the road, and he is among the people of Paradise. When the people alighted upon me, some of them began gesturing to others and looking at me, so I said: What is with you? You gesture to one another and look at me? They said: Rejoice with the glad tidings of Allah and His Messenger, for we recognize in you the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They informed me of what he had said to them, so I fed them, gave them drink, provisioned them, and went out with them until I guided them to the road. Then I returned to my family and bequeathed to them regarding my camels, then I went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: To what do you call? He said: I call to testifying that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan. I said: If we answer you to this, are we safe regarding our families, our blood, and our wealth? He said: Yes. So I became Muslim, returned to my people, informed them of my Islam, and many people among them became Muslim at my hands. Then I emigrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While I was with him one day, he said to me: O Amr, would you like me to show you a sign of Paradise? He eats food, drinks drink, and walks in the markets. I said: Yes, may my father be ransom for you. He said: This one and his people are a sign of Paradise, and he pointed to Ali ibn Abi Talib. And he said to me: O Amr, would you like me to show you a sign of the Fire? He eats food, drinks drink, and walks in the markets? I said: Yes, may my father be ransom for you. He said: This one and his people are a sign of the Fire, and he pointed to a man. When the tribulation occurred, I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I fled from the sign of the Fire to the sign of Paradise. And do you see Banu Umayyah killing me after this? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: By Allah, if I were in a hole within a hole, Banu Umayyah would extract me until they kill me; my beloved the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me that: That my head is the first head to be severed in Islam, and carried from land to land. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith except Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"4087","4082 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hibarah ibn Lakhm al-Iskandarani narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to turn in prayer to his right and to his left; then Allah revealed: {Successful indeed are the believers * Those who are humble in their prayers}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became humble and would not turn to the right or to the left. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Jarir, nor from Jarir except Ibn Wahb; Hibarah was alone in transmitting it."
"4088","4083 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away at the age of sixty-three, and Abu Bakr at the age of sixty-three, and Umar at the age of sixty-three. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zubayr except Uthman ibn Zaidah; al-Hakam was alone in transmitting it."
"4089","4084 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Jafar ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The two ears are part of the head. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ashath except Ali; Ali ibn Ziyad was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"4090","4085 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ubaydillah ibn al-Hasan al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Nafi al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, he said: A man would sacrifice a single sheep on behalf of himself and his household; then the people vied with one another, and it became a display. No one narrated this hadith from Malik, from al-Zuhri, except Abdillah; Ahmad ibn Ubaydillah was alone in transmitting it."
"4091","4086 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Raja al-Utaridi say: I heard Ibn Abbas narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The affair of this umma will remain close together - or he said: harmonious - so long as they do not speak about children and predestination. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Raja except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"4092","4087 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Tawbah al-Qazwini narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Mualla ibn Irfan, from Abu Wail, from Abdillah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness is good fortune, and harshness is ill omen. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mualla except Muhammad; Ismail was alone in transmitting it."
"4093","4088 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Salih, the freedman of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray between Zhuhr and Asr. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Abu Khalid; Tahir ibn Abi Ahmad was alone in transmitting it."
"4094","4089 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Shawkar narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Israil, from Maysarah ibn Habib, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: I have not seen anyone among Allah's creation more resembling the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in religion, sitting, or walking than Fatimah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, she welcomed him, rose from her seat, kissed his hand, and seated him in her seat; and when she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he welcomed her, rose to her, kissed her hand, and seated her in his seat. And she entered upon him while he was in his house, and he confided to her, so she wept; then he confided to her again, so she laughed. Aishah said: I said to the women: I used to think this woman had merit over women, while she weeps then she laughs. I asked her afterwards: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confide to you? She did not tell me. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, I asked her, and she said: He said: I shall die in this illness of mine. So I grieved and wept; and he confided to me that I am the first of his family to join him, so I was gladdened by that and laughed. No one narrated this hadith from Israil except Uthman ibn Umar and Ismail ibn Jafar."
"4095","4090 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Uthman ibn Abi al-As, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed wine, its drinker, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the eater of its price. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Abdillah ibn Isa; Uqbah ibn Mukram was alone in transmitting it."
"4096","4091 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Abi al-Rabab narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Rashid, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of earthen jars, then permitted it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Yahya; Damrah was alone in transmitting it."
"4097","4092 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Khabbab, he said: I heard Abu al-Khalil narrating to Mujahid, he said: Mutarrif ibn Abdillah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to us, he said: The first commander to address us at Basra was Utbah ibn Ghazwan al-Sulami, and he was the first to settle it as a garrison town, and he was noble. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: This world has announced its severance and turned away swiftly, and there remains of it only a remnant like the remnant of a vessel; and you are moving from this abode, so move with the best of what is at hand. It has reached me that a stone is thrown from the edge of Hell and does not reach its bottom for forty years - are you not amazed? By Allah, it will surely be filled. And it has reached me that between two leaves of the gates of Paradise is forty years, yet by Allah there will come upon it a day crowded with throngs. I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the seventh of seven, and our mouths had become cracked from eating trees. I saw myself and Sad splitting a cloak into two halves; I wore half of it and Sad wore half of it. And there is none among us today but that he is a commander over a city among these cities. And it has reached me that there was no prophethood but that it was abrogated into kingship; and I seek refuge with Allah from being great in myself and small in the eyes of people. And you will try commanders after me. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Abu al-Khalil, nor from Abu al-Khalil except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Amr; Abbad ibn Yaqub was alone in transmitting it."
"4098","4093 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Salamah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sirmah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, the freedman of Ibn Ayyash, narrated to me, from Irak ibn Malik, from Aishah, she said: A poor woman carrying her two sons came to me, so I fed her three dates; she gave each of her two sons a date, and raised a date to her mouth to eat it, but her two sons asked her for food, so she split the date she had intended to eat between them. Her affair impressed me, so I mentioned her and what she had done to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Allah has indeed made Paradise obligatory for her, and freed her from the Fire."
"4099","4094 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I declare sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah, as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Ibrahim ibn Sirmah."
"4100","4095 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam informed us, from Israil, from Said ibn Masruq, from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last seven. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Masruq except Israil; Musab ibn al-Miqdam was alone in transmitting it."
"4101","4096 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Mihraqani narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Aidh, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Ayyub, nor from Ayyub except Abdillah."
"4102","4097 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Mawhab ibn Yazid ibn Mawhab al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Dharr, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he took pebbles and they glorified Allah in his hand; then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he took them and they glorified Allah in his hand; then he gave them to Abu Bakr, and they glorified Allah in his hand. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took them, and they glorified Allah in his hand; then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he gave them to Umar, and they glorified Allah in his hand. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took them, and they glorified Allah in his hand; then he put them down and they fell silent. Then he gave them to Uthman, and they glorified Allah in his hand. Then he gave them to Ali, and he placed them in his hand and they fell silent. Al-Zuhri said: It is the caliphate which Allah gave Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, except Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, nor from Ibn Abi Humayd except Ibn Wahb; Mawhab was alone in transmitting it."
"4103","4098 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Bayan narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer, then turned, faced the people, and said: O Allah, bless for us our Madinah, bless for us our mudd and our sa, O Allah, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen. A man said: And Iraq, O Messenger of Allah? He fell silent, then said: O Allah, bless for us our Madinah, bless for us our mudd and our sa, O Allah, bless for us our sanctuary, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen. A man said: And Iraq, O Messenger of Allah? He said: From there the horn of Satan rises, and tribulations rage. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Bayan except Ismail ibn Ulayyah; his son Hammad was alone in transmitting it."
"4104","4099 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Mualla narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, from Salim ibn Abdillah, from Abdillah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will alight at this salt flat, and most of those who go out to him will be women, to the extent that a man will go to his beloved - whether his mother, his sister, or his wife - and bind her tightly lest she join him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then they will be given power over him and over his party - and his party are the Jews - and will kill them, until one of them hides behind a stone or a tree, and the stone or the tree will say: O believer, behind me is a Jew, so kill him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Talhah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn al-Mualla was alone in transmitting it."
"4105","4100 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Buraydah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Are the stones and the trees many? - three times. We said: Yes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my intercession is indeed more numerous than the stones and the trees. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Buraydah except with this chain; Abu Jabir was alone in transmitting it."
"4106","4101 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth will never be without forty men like Ibrahim, the friend of the Merciful; through them they are given rain and through them they are given victory; no sooner does one of them die than Allah replaces another in his place. He said: And I heard Qatadah say: We do not doubt that al-Hasan is among them. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said, nor from Said except Abd al-Wahhab; Ishaq was alone in transmitting it."
"4107","4102 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Shuayb ibn Ishaq al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai and Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, he said: Aishah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a dead land, it belongs to him. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said to him: Do you testify that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this? He said: I testify that Aishah narrated this to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I testify that Aishah did not lie to me. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"4108","4103 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Bashir ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Durayk, from Yala ibn Munabbih, raising the hadith to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah will raise a black, dark cloud for the people of the Fire, and it will be said: O people of the Fire, what do you seek? They will remember by it the cloud of this world, and say: O our Lord, drink. So He will rain upon them fetters that increase their fetters, chains that increase their chains, and embers that blaze upon them. This hadith is not narrated from Yala except with this chain; Mansur was alone in transmitting it."
"4109","4104 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uqbah ibn Alqamah al-Bayruti narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibn Shawdhab narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to me, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for blessing in the pre-dawn meal. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Shawdhab except Uqbah; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"4110","4105 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: Aswad ibn Hafs al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Yazid al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a journey, he would kiss his daughter Fatimah. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid al-Nahwi except al-Husayn ibn Waqid, nor from al-Husayn except Aswad ibn Hafs and Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"4111","4106 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ali al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: That al-Najashi gave Umm Habibah a dowry on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of two hundred dinars. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Rawwad was alone in transmitting it."
"4112","4107 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you were to lower one of you with a rope to the seventh earth, he would come upon his Lord, Mighty and Majestic. Then he recited: {He is the First and the Last, the Manifest and the Hidden, and He is Knowing of all things}. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Jafar, nor from Abu Jafar except Salamah; al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi was alone in transmitting it."
"4113","4108 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in the quantity of a faraq, a sip of it is unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abu Jafar al-Razi; Salamah ibn al-Fadl was alone in transmitting it."
"4114","4109 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Nafi Abu Hajar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdillah al-Narmaqi narrated to us, he said: Yahya al-Bakka narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn Umar say: A man belched in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Restrain your belching, for the longest of you in satiety in this world will be the longest of you in hunger on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Abd al-Aziz al-Narmaqi was alone in transmitting it."
"4115","4110 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Mahmawayh ibn Shuja al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna narrated to me, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abdillah say: Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to me, that he was sitting at the base of the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he addressed the people, when a man from the desert folk came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the night prayer? He said: Yes, two by two; then when you fear that dawn will overtake you or catch you, you bow one rakah, and it makes odd for you what has passed."
"4116","4110 م - Ali narrated to us, he said: Mahmawayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, he said: We came to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr and asked him, and he narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith which Salim narrated to us. No one narrated this hadith from Salim and al-Qasim except Abu Ubaydah."
"4117","4111 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Asim al-Bajali, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever does not press his nose along with his forehead to the ground in his prostration, his prayer is not accepted. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn Zadham except al-Dahhak; Muhammad ibn Himyar was alone in transmitting it. And Asim al-Bajali is Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal."
"4118","4112 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn Khalid, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab employed Muadh over Sham, and wrote to him: Give the people their stipends, and raid with them. While he was giving the people, at the end of the day, a man from the people of the countryside came from such-and-such place and said to him: O Muadh, who will get me my stipend? For I am a man from the countryside, from such-and-such place, and perhaps I may shelter with my family before night? He said: By Allah, I shall not give you until I give these, meaning the people of the city. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: All the prophets will enter Paradise two thousand years before Dawud and Sulayman; and the poor Muslims will enter Paradise forty years before their rich; and righteous slaves will enter Paradise forty years before free men; and the people of cities will enter Paradise forty years before the people of villages, for cities excel by Friday prayer, congregations, and circles of remembrance, and when there is affliction they are singled out with it to the exclusion of them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Shuayb, nor narrated it from Shuayb except Amr, nor narrated it from Amr except Harun, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"4119","4113 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Maymun al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: When did you pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: While the sun was white and clear. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Abdillah."
"4120","4114 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Atiyyah ibn Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not abandon the night prayer, even for the milking of a sheep. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Munkadir except Jarir ibn Yazid; Baqiyyah was alone in transmitting it."
"4121","4115 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, and from Ibn Abi Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Makkah, and he kept shortening the prayer until we arrived at Makkah, where he stayed ten days shortening the prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Thawri, from Yunus, except Ayyub."
"4122","4116 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdah ibn Sulayman al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): War is deception. No one narrated this hadith as connected, from Abdah, except his son Muhammad."
"4123","4117 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Zadham, from Abdillah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined between Zhuhr and Asr, and between Maghrib and Isha. He was asked about that, and said: I did this so that my umma would not be put to hardship. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abdillah, nor narrated it from Abdillah except al-Husayn and Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil."
"4124","4118 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from Ibn Aidh, from Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Ayyub Khalid ibn Zayd, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever meets the enemy and is patient until he is killed or overcomes, he will not be tried in his grave. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from Abu Ayyub, except with this chain; Munabbih ibn Uthman was alone in transmitting it."
"4125","4119 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Ibrahim ibn Mathrud narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Iyad, from Abu Hazim, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches the rakah has caught the prostration. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Yazid ibn Iyad, nor from Yazid except Ibn Wahb; Isa ibn Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"4126","4120 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Rasi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taraifi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Aradah narrated to me, from Abu Masud al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were struck by hunger in his time, so two men came until they overlooked some walled gardens, and there were dates in a garden. One of them descended and the other stayed back out of fear; he ate until full, then began scooping into his clothes. The owner of the garden came, snatched his garment, tied him to a palm tree, took a splinter and beat him painfully, then took him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I found this one in my garden; he ate until full, then began scooping into his clothes. The other said: O Messenger of Allah, my companion and I came hungry; as for me, I descended, and as for my companion, he stayed back out of fear. I ate and took for my companion. This one came and did such-and-such to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go, give him his garment, and measure for him a wasq in place of your beating him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Abdillah ibn Aradah; Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain."
"4127","4121 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Qatadah al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Salim ibn Ghaylan, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies owing fasts, his guardian fasts on his behalf. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Haywah; Abu Qatadah was alone in transmitting it."
"4128","4122 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: My uncle Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Samh narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Maymun, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheists wear shirts and do not wear lower garments? He said: You wear shirts and wear lower garments. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheists go barefoot and do not wear sandals? He said: Go barefoot and wear sandals; oppose the allies of Satan as much as you can. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Khalid, nor from Khalid except Abdillah, nor from Abdillah except Ibn Wahb; his nephew was alone in transmitting it."
"4129","4123 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the believer falls ill, Allah purifies him as the bellows purifies the dross of iron. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ibn Abi Dhib; Ibn Abi Fudayk was alone in transmitting it."
"4130","4124 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Muawiyah al-Bazzar al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sallam al-Ifriqi narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Nahik, from Yala ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever gives respite to one in difficulty or gives charity to him, Allah will shade him in His shade on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Yala ibn Shaddad except Ayyub ibn Nahik; Yahya ibn Sallam was alone in transmitting it."
"4131","4125 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Harun al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Abbas, that Muawiyah prayed Asr, then Ibn al-Zubayr stood and prayed after it. Muawiyah said: O Ibn Abbas, what are these two rakahs? He said: An innovation, and its doer is an innovator. When he turned, he said: What did you two say? He said: We said such-and-such. He said: I did not innovate, but my maternal aunt Aishah narrated to me. So Muawiyah sent to Aishah, and she said: He spoke the truth; Umm Salamah narrated to me. So he sent to Umm Salamah that Aishah narrated to us from you such-and-such? She said: She spoke the truth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me one day and prayed after Asr; I stood behind him and prayed. When he turned, he said: What is with you? I said: I saw you, O Prophet of Allah, pray, so I prayed with you. He said: A collector of charities came to me, and I feared for him, so I met him, and forgot to pray two rakahs after Asr. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said; Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd was alone in transmitting it."
"4132","4126 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing between a man and polytheism and disbelief except abandoning prayer."
"4133","4127 - And with the same chain, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The throne of Iblis is upon the sea; then he sends his detachments and they cause tribulation, and the greatest among them in his sight is the greatest among them in tribulation. No one narrated these two hadiths from Qatadah, from Sulayman, except Said, nor from Said except Musab; Abu Kurayb was alone in transmitting them both."
"4134","4128 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibn Abi Layla."
"4135","4129 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Ayan narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abdillah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command them to pray at seven years, and strike them for it at thirteen. No one narrated this hadith from Thumamah except al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"4136","4130 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among a group of the Emigrants and the Helpers; Ali ibn Abi Talib was on his left and al-Abbas on his right, when al-Abbas and a man from the Helpers quarreled, and the Helper spoke harshly to al-Abbas. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of al-Abbas and the hand of Ali and said: There will emerge from the loins of this one a people who will fill the earth with tyranny and injustice, and there will emerge from the loins of this one a people who will fill the earth with justice and equity. When you see that, then hold to the Tamimi youth, for he will come from the east and he is the bearer of the banner of the Mahdi. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Umar except Ibn Lahiah; Kathir ibn Jafar was alone in transmitting it."
"4137","4131 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Anbasah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Qazaah ibn Yahya, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best jihad before Allah on the Day of Resurrection belongs to those who meet in the rank and do not turn their faces until they are killed; those wallow in the highest chambers of Paradise. Your Lord looks at them; indeed when your Lord laughs to a people, there is no reckoning upon them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Ibn al-Mubarak, nor from Ibn al-Mubarak except Anbasah; Said ibn Yahya was alone in transmitting it."
"4138","4132 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, he said: I heard Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every lineage and marriage tie will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection, except my lineage and my marriage tie. This hadith is not narrated from Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Umar was alone in transmitting it."
"4139","4133 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abdillah narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abbad ibn Yahya ibn Khallad al-Zuraqi narrated to me, he said: We entered upon Abdillah ibn Unays, and he said: Shall I not show you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, and how he prayed? We said: Yes. So he washed his hands three times each, rinsed his mouth and nose three times, washed his face and his arms to the elbows three times each, wiped his head forward and backward, touched his ears, and washed his feet three times each. Then he took a garment, wrapped himself in it, and prayed. And he said: Thus I saw my beloved the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and pray. It is not narrated from Abdillah ibn Unays except with this chain; Zayd ibn al-Hubab was alone in transmitting it."
"4140","4134 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn Jabir al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Abu Hashim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Khidash al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Masad ibn Uqbah, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned the spoils on the slain to the killer. No one narrated this hadith from Masad ibn Uqbah except Umar ibn Ayyub; Abu Hashim was alone in transmitting it."
"4141","4135 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abu Hashim al-Wasiti, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he prayed over the dead he would say: O Allah, You created him, You guided him to Islam, You took his soul, and You know best his secret and his open; we have come to intercede for him, so accept our intercession for him. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; al-Hasan ibn Hammad was alone in transmitting it. And Yahya ibn Abbad is Abu Hubayrah al-Makhzumi."
"4142","4136 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abi Azzah, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from Abu Ayyub, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us food, he would partake of it; then he sent us food and did not partake of it. I said: This is food from which you did not partake. He said: In it is a herb I dislike, so eat it. I said: I dislike what you dislike. No one narrated this hadith from Isa ibn Abi Azzah except Israil; Abd al-Razzaq was alone in transmitting it."
"4143","4137 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl ibn Husayn Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar - al-Barra - Yusuf ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Awsajah al-Tamimi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Furat al-Qazzaz narrated to me, from Abu Hazim al-Ashjai, from Muhammad ibn Durayh al-Ashjai, he said: I narrate to you only what my ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); had I heard it only once, or twice, or three times, or four, or five, or six, or seven times, I would have thought I would not narrate it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are upon unity, and one comes to split your unity and break your staff, then kill him, whoever among people he may be. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Furat, nor narrated it from Furat except Abu Mashar; Abu Kamil was alone in transmitting it."
"4144","4138 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Sulayman ibn Mihran, from Abu Wail, from Abdillah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit us with admonition on some days, out of fear of boring us. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except al-Salt ibn Masud."
"4145","4139 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hafs al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers after me who will lead you in prayer; if they complete its bowing and prostration, it is for you and for them, and if they fall short, it is for you and against them. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, except Attaf ibn Khalid; Ali ibn Hafs al-Madaini was alone in transmitting it. And Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Misri and others narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abu Ali al-Hamdani Thumamah ibn Shufi, from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"4146","4140 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Isa al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is written for him; if he does it, ten are written up to what Allah wills. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is written against him; if he does it, one is written against him, or Allah effaces it. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn Zadham except Hushaym, nor from Hushaym except al-Qasim, and Amr ibn Awn."
"4147","4141 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Bashir al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The right of a Muslim upon a Muslim is five: if he falls ill, visit him; if he dies, attend his funeral; if he passes by, greet him; if he sneezes, bless him; and if he invites him, even to a trotter, accept. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except al-Sabbah ibn Muharib. And Said is al-Maqburi, and it is said: Said ibn Mina."
"4148","4142 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Ali al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from Simak ibn Harb, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you buy gold with silver, do not part from him while there is any confusion between you and him."
"4149","4143 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Abu Khalid, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Masud, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a small red bird passing over the heads of his Companions and said: Who has bereaved this one? A man from the Ansar said: I, O Messenger of Allah; I took eggs of hers, or chicks. So he commanded him and he returned them. No one narrated these hadiths from Abu Khalid except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it."
"4150","4144 - And with the same chain, from Abu Khalid, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, like for like; whoever increases or seeks increase has dealt in usury. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the keeper of your dates buys a sa for two sa. So he sent to him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, my dates are such-and-such, and they do not take them unless I give them extra. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah except Abu Khalid, nor narrated it from Abu Khalid except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it, and Abu Ghassan al-Nahdi."
"4151","4145 - And with the same chain, from Abu Khalid, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from Ribiy ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I was given the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Abu Khalid, nor from Abu Khalid except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it."
"4152","4146 - And with the same chain: from Abu Khalid, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, from Ayyub al-Harithi, he said: I heard Amr ibn al-As say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever repents before his death by the milking of a she-camel, Allah will turn to him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalid except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Amr ibn al-As except with this chain."
"4153","4147 - And with the same chain: Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, and al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about stoning the jamrahs: What is for us in it? I heard him say: You will find that with your Lord when you are most in need of it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah except Hajjaj, nor from Hajjaj except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it."
"4154","4148 - And with the same chain, from Abu Khalid, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah only aids the Muslims through the supplication of the weak. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Murrah except Abu Khalid, nor from Abu Khalid except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it."
"4155","4149 - And with the same chain: Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Woe to the heels from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abd al-Salam; Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it."
"4156","4150 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf al-Attar al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sulami narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People are from diverse trees, and I and Ali are from one tree. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil except Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sulami, nor from Muhammad ibn Ali except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar; Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf was alone in transmitting it."
"4157","4151 - Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Khazzaz narrated to us, at Rayy, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Imran ibn Sulayman, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: By Allah, we did not recognize our hypocrites in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by their hatred of Ali. No one narrated this hadith from Imran ibn Sulayman al-Qubbi except Amr; Muhammad ibn Hassan was alone in transmitting it."
"4158","4152 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Furat ibn Muhammad al-Qayrawani narrated to us, he said: Shajarah ibn Isa al-Maafiri narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Karimah, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trade with the wealth of orphans, lest zakat consume it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Umarah, nor from Umarah except Abd al-Malik, nor from Abd al-Malik except Shajarah, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"4159","4153 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Sahl ibn Bassam al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Musab, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is forbidden to all nations until I enter it, I and my umma, the first then the first. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Kharijah, nor from Kharijah except Abdan."
"4160","4154 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Qanab ibn Muhriz ibn Qanab al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Asmai narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Abdah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A caller will call in the Fire: O Compassionate, O Bestower. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Abdah except al-Asmai; Qanab ibn Muhriz ibn Qanab was alone in transmitting it."
"4161","4155 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Hubayrah Yahya ibn Abbad, he said: I heard Tamim al-Dari say: A skin of wine was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after it had been forbidden. When it was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wine has indeed been forbidden. Some said: Would that they sold it and gave its price to the poor Muslims? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding it, and it was poured out in a valley among the valleys of Madinah, and said: Allah has cursed the Jews; its fats were forbidden to them, yet they sold them and ate their prices. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath, from Abu Hubayrah, except al-Sabbah ibn Muharib."
"4162","4156 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Wabisi al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, he said: Sayyar, the freedman of Iyad, narrated to me, from Wabisah ibn Mabad al-Asadi, he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Farewell Pilgrimage while he addressed and said: O people, which month is most sacred? They said: This month. He said: Which day is most sacred? They said: This day, and it is the day of sacrifice. He said: Which land is greatest in sanctity before Allah? They said: This one. He said: Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are forbidden to you on this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours, until the day you meet your Lord. Have I not conveyed? The people said: Yes. He raised his hands to heaven, then said: O Allah, bear witness. Then he said: O people, have I not conveyed? They said: Yes. He raised his hands to heaven, then said: O Allah, bear witness. Then he said: Let the witness among you convey to the absent. Wabisah said: We witnessed and you were absent, and we convey to you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. This hadith is not narrated from Wabisah except with this chain; Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Rahman was alone in transmitting it."
"4163","4157 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Imran al-Isbahani narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal al-Bajali narrated to us, from his father, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Abu Yahya, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman should not touch another woman in one cloth but that they are both adulteresses, and a man should not touch another man but that they are both adulterers. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Abu Dawud was alone in transmitting it. And Abu Yahya from whom Anas ibn Sirin narrated in this hadith is Mabad ibn Sirin."
"4164","4158 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Khalil al-Kalai al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Thawban, the judge of Hims, narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah: That Bilal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the call for the dawn prayer and found him sleeping, so he called out: Prayer is better than sleep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not disapprove of it and entered it into the call to prayer; no call is made for a prayer before its time except the dawn prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Numan; Marwan was alone in transmitting it."
"4165","4159 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah ibn al-Birind al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with an old man, and he said: O so-and-so, who is this with you? He said: My father. He said: Do not walk in front of him, do not sit before him, do not call him by his name, and do not cause him to be reviled. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan; Amr ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"4166","4160 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad Muawiyah ibn Wahib ibn Sawwar al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: My uncle Unays ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first to enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and I shall intercede; and men from my umma will meet Isa son of Maryam and witness the battle against the Dajjal."
"4167","4161 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Wahib ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: My uncle Unays narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to raid in the pre-Islamic period; what do you command us? He said: Slaughter in whatever month it may be, be dutiful to Allah, and feed. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Unays; Muawiyah ibn Wahib was alone in transmitting it."
"4168","4162 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Salim al-Anumi, from Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment, he would say: Raid in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not steal from spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child, a woman, or an old man. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir ibn Zayd except Amr ibn Harim, nor from Amr except Salim; al-Sabbah was alone in transmitting it."
"4169","4163 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Nubatah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, he said: Ali said to Abu al-Hayyaj: Shall I send you upon what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me upon? He said: Leave no raised grave but that you level it, nor any image but that you efface it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Amr ibn Abi Qays; Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz was alone in transmitting it."
"4170","4164 - Ali ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Ashhal ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ubaydillah ibn al-Qibtiyyah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An army will be swallowed up in a desert tract of the earth. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Ibn Awn, nor from Ibn Awn except Ashhal; Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr was alone in transmitting it."
"4171","4165 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The child of adultery bears none of the sin of his parents. Then he recited: {And no bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another}. No one raised this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri except Abbad ibn al-Awwam; Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Madaini was alone in transmitting it."
"4172","4166 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abi Khidash al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: My uncle Abu Hashim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Khidash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Mihsan, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Do not turn back after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others; a man is not seized for the offense of his brother nor for the offense of his father. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn Mihsan, and he is al-Ukashi, from the offspring of Ukashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi; Ibn Abi Khidash al-Mawsili was alone in transmitting it."
"4173","4167 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurrah Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Ruayni narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from al-Ala ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Abu Burdah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever conceals testimony when called to it is like one who testifies falsely. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except al-Ala, nor from al-Ala except Muawiyah, nor from Muawiyah except Abdillah ibn Salih; Abu Qurrah was alone in transmitting it."
"4174","4168 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Mumin narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Ubaydah al-Naji narrated to us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him. No one narrated this hadith from Bahz ibn Hakim except Zakariyya ibn Abi Ubaydah; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Mumin was alone in transmitting it."
"4175","4169 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalaf ibn Ishaq ibn Mirsal al-Khathami narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Harun, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever points at his brother with a piece of iron, the angels continue to curse him until he puts it down, even if he is his full brother. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala except Damrah ibn Rabiah."
"4176","4170 - Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muthanna al-Juhani al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Ibrahim on the night I was taken by night; he said: O Muhammad, convey peace to your umma, and inform them that Paradise is of good soil and sweet water, and that it is plains, and its plantings are the saying: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and there is no might nor power except with Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Masud except from the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Qasim."
"4177","4171 - Ali ibn Amr al-Wasiti al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abdillah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Amr and Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya except Hushaym; Muhammad ibn Khalid was alone in transmitting it."
"4178","4172 - Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Amiri al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym Dirar ibn Surad al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibn Shihab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, regarding His saying: {Then He sent down upon you, after grief, security as slumber}: He said: Sleep was cast upon us on the day of Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"4179","4173 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Dirar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to test the believing women who emigrated to him with this verse: {O Prophet, when the believing women come to you}.. the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Wahid except Abd al-Aziz."
"4180","4174 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Akfani narrated to us, he said: Khunays ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Bakr and Umar are the chiefs of the elderly of the people of Paradise among the first and the last, apart from the prophets and the messengers. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Khunays; Zakariyya ibn Yahya was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abi Juhayfah except with this chain."
"4181","4175 - Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet? He said: While Adam was between spirit and body. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Nasr ibn Muzahim was alone in transmitting it."
"4182","4176 - Ali ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that he was in the house of Maymunah, and placed purification water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who placed it? It was said: Ibn Abbas. So he struck my shoulder and said: O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except al-Qasim; Muqaddam was alone in transmitting it."
"4183","4177 - Ali ibn Jabalah al-Baghdadi al-Katib narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns archery then forgets it, it is a blessing he has denied."
"4184","4178 - Ali ibn Jabalah al-Isbahani narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Ibrahim Bardan ibn Abi al-Nadr, the freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydillah ibn Mamar, from his father, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man's prayer in his house is better than his prayer in this mosque of mine, except the obligatory. Bardan ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated no hadith with a chain except this one; Ismail ibn Abi Uways was alone in transmitting it."
"4185","4179 - Ali ibn Ishaq al-Wazir al-Isbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Awsi narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Abdillah ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield from the Fire; whoever begins the morning fasting should not act ignorantly that day, and if a man acts ignorantly toward him, let him not revile or abuse him, but say: I am fasting. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter before Allah than the scent of musk. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ruman except Kharijah; Man was alone in transmitting it."
"4186","4180 - Ali ibn Rustum al-Isbahani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muawiyah al-Isbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad, meaning al-Isbahani, narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us; they said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim say: al-Mustawrid, brother of Banu Fihr, narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By Allah, this world from its beginning to its end is only like one of you placing his finger in the sea; let him see what it returns with. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except al-Numan."
"4187","4181 - Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked, when he went out for a need, to hear: O Najih, O Rashid. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Abu Amir; Muhammad ibn Rafi was alone in transmitting it."
"4188","4182 - Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Rushdyn ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he performed ablution wipe his face with the edge of his garment. This hadith is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain; Rushdyn was alone in transmitting it."
"4189","4183 - Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Abdillah al-Attar al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Isa al-Sijzi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hasten to good, walk barefoot, for Allah multiplies its reward over the shod. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Sulayman; Yusuf was alone in transmitting it."
"4190","4184 - Ali ibn Muhammad al-Ansari al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that they were one day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a dish of bread and meat from the house of Umm Salamah, and it was placed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Put your hands. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his hand, and we put our hands, and ate. He said: And Aishah was preparing food hastily, having seen the dish that had been brought. When she finished her food, she brought it, placed it, took up the dish of Umm Salamah and broke it, and said and said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat, in the name of Allah; your mother has felt jealousy. Then he gave her dish to Umm Salamah, and said: Food for food, and vessel for vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah except Yahya, nor from Yahya except Ibn Wahb; Harmalah was alone in transmitting it."
"4191","4185 - Ali ibn Abd al-Samad al-Tayalisi Allan Maghammah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hatim; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi was alone in transmitting it."
"4192","4186 - Ali ibn Abd al-Samad al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Hatim al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Sahl al-Sarraj, al-Rabi ibn Subayh, Wasil, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman, Yazid ibn Ibrahim, and Hisham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment? He said: And do all of you find two garments? No one narrated this hadith from Sahl al-Sarraj and al-Rabi ibn Subayh except Yahya; Ishaq ibn Hatim was alone in transmitting it."
"4193","4187 - Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Himyari narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Tahhan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters but that he chose the easier of them. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Sahl."
"4194","4188 - Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Dabbas narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of Friday has caught it, except that he make up what he missed. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Abd al-Aziz; Ibrahim was alone in transmitting it."
"4195","4189 - Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Hanbali al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or a vessel of silver, he only gargles fire in his belly. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Burd ibn Sinan, Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, and Abdillah ibn Amir al-Aslami. And Malik ibn Anas, Ubaydillah ibn Umar, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, and the people narrated it from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdillah ibn Umar, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her."
"4196","4190 - Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Thaqafi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn al-Haytham ibn al-Rayyan al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Khurasani narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in the end of time unjust rulers, wicked ministers, treacherous judges, and lying jurists; whoever among you reaches that time, let him not be a collector for them, nor a headman, nor a policeman. This hadith is not narrated from Qatadah except with this chain."
"4197","4191 - Ali ibn Uthman ibn Ubaydah al-Fazari al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Masud ibn Juwayriyah al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Wasit ibn al-Harith, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine until he dies, it will be forbidden to him in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Wasit ibn al-Harith."
"4198","4192 - Ali ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn al-Shair narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Israil ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No talebearer will enter Paradise; and the talebearer is the slanderer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except Israil, nor from Israil except Abu Ahmad; Hajjaj was alone in transmitting it."
"4199","4193 - Ali ibn Ishaq ibn Zatiya al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, he said: Faraj ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I would miss days of Ramadan fasting, and would not make them up except in Shaban."
"4200","4194 - Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani Tughk narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hadhdha narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Said, from Thabit, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated, he raised his hands until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen. No one narrated this hadith from Said except Baqiyyah."
